{"name": "Bestial Creature", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are considered both Humanoid and Beast when it comes to rules affecting creatures types.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "A69S7OIOQPX7A5GA", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Beseech Providence", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/people/cleric-orange.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are no stranger to setting an example of your faith, both in your deeds and in your words. You have advantage on Presence (Persuasion) checks made to implore someone to carry out a selfless act that is at most inconvenient to them (such as helping a neighbor rebuild their shed or donating a small amount to a starving creature).</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "background", "subtype": ""}, "requirements": "Early Devotee", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": "Background Features", "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "CZKRUMYCK6X1L5WN", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Choose Your Battles", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/people/infantry-army.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>The supreme art of war is to subdue the enemy without fighting. You have advantage on Presence (Intimidation) checks made to convince others to back down from a fight with you.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "background", "subtype": ""}, "requirements": "Early Militant", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": "Background Features", "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "QJK4VRMK8IZWD41C", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Connected", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/diplomacy-handshake-gray.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Any time you enter a city or town and have spent at least a day there, you know how to get in contact with those who deal in shady business, and how to get a friendly introduction.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "background", "subtype": ""}, "requirements": "Early Scoundrel", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "QECKCO8JGKG5L6Z9", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Eye for Quality", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/trades/textiles-cloth-dye-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are skilled at appraising any non-magical object that could be crafted by a trade you are proficient with. You have advantage on checks to determine the base price of these crafts and identify forgeries. You also learn whether the object you are appraising is magical, but not what its effects are.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "background", "subtype": ""}, "requirements": "Early Artisan", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": "Background Features", "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "5Z5KEPS9RQKUVCPC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "A Helping Hand", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/wave-halt-stop.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>The first time you ask for an object or help from someone whom you have helped before, they are heavily inclined to oblige. In the situation where a Presence (Persuasion) check is required, you have advantage on the check.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "background", "subtype": ""}, "requirements": "Early Humanitarian", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": "Background Features", "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "XRDOHUHF3RTLV18F", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Institutional Sway", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/brooch-crown-gold.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your insignia and general air distinguish you from the unwashed masses, making bureaucrats and authority figures less likely to dismiss your concerns. Should you need to arrange an audience or appointment, you have advantage on Presence (Persuasion) checks to do so.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "background", "subtype": ""}, "requirements": "Early Aristocrat", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": "Background Features", "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2BWN854LL0WQ39J3", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Know the Ropes", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/settlement/ship.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are no stranger to the workings of a ship. You can easily negotiate passage on a ship for you and your companions in exchange for labor during the voyage, provided the ship has enough excess capacity to accommodate you. Should the crew require convincing, you have advantage on the associated Presence (Persuasion) checks.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "background", "subtype": ""}, "requirements": "Early Sailor", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": "Background Features", "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "6S8K0D2XXAKPWE4J", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Lay of the Land", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/wilderness/tree-oak.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are familiar with traveling the land and fending for yourself.  When traveling in the wilderness you can easily find food and water for yourself and a handful of other people.  As well, you get advantage on Intelligence (Nature) checks to determine whether a plant is edible and safe to consume, and whether water is safe to drink.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "background", "subtype": ""}, "requirements": "Early Outsider", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": "Background Features", "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "U8KK1AON39A2OHR2", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Prepared", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-writing-brown-gold.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Should you spend your next short or long rest studying an object, creature, or event, you gain advantage on the next Intelligence or Wisdom based roll you make, excluding Wisdom (Instinct), to understand something about the subject.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "background", "subtype": ""}, "requirements": "Early Scholar", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": "Background Features", "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "CEDNUQ4BN37WPXPH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Number of Chaos", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/clover-luck-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain a new Eikonic Number which serves as your <strong>Eikonic Number of Chaos</strong> (see the &ldquo;Eikonic Numbers&rdquo; Cleric Starter Ability for details).</p><p>You also gain access to the following <strong>Mantras</strong>, which can only be assigned to your <strong>Eikonic Number of Chaos</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Chaotic:</strong> You can immediately either:</li><ul><li>Cause a small object to move a few feet.</li><li>Cause a small fragile object to crack or shatter.</li><li>Swap places with a creature up to 10ft away.</li></ul><li><strong>Control of Chaos:</strong> You can re-roll 1 die before the end of your next turn, and must take the new result.</li><li><strong>Embrace the Chaos:</strong> A creature of your choice that you can see takes 1d10 chaos damage. You take half of the damage dealt, unless you spend a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith} Die to negate the damage against yourself.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": "?", "style": "single", "name": "Eikon: Chaos", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": "?", "rechargeOn": "none", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "7RQ8BN29ZKQKDDPV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Flux Mindset", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/clover-luck-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you take a rest, roll on the <em>Flux Proficiency Table</em>.&nbsp; Based on the result, you gain proficiency in that skill until your next long rest, after your new proficiency has been decided by this ability.&nbsp; Re-roll on the table if you land on any proficiency you already possess.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Flux Proficiency Table</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>1d20</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Proficiency</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Athletics</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Acrobatics</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>Stealth</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>Sleight of Hand</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>Arcana</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>Craft</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>Culture</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>Investigation</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>Nature</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>Insight</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>11</p></td><td><p>Instinct</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>12</p></td><td><p>Medicine</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>13</p></td><td><p>Perception</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>14</p></td><td><p>Theology</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>15</p></td><td><p>Deception</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>16</p></td><td><p>Intimidation</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>17</p></td><td><p>Perform</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>18</p></td><td><p>Persuasion</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>19</p></td><td><p>Pick a Tool Proficiency</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>20</p></td><td><p>Pick any Skill or Tool Proficiency</p></td></tr></tbody></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": "", "style": "choice", "name": "Flux Mindset", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "short", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "Reroll every rest.", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "flux-mindset", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": ["Athletics", "Acrobatics", "Stealth", "Sleight of Hand", "Arcana", "Craft", "Culture", "Investigation", "Nature", "Insight", "Instinct", "Medicine", "Perception", "Theology", "Deception", "Intimidation", "Perform", "Persuasion", "Trade Proficiency"]}}, "folder": null, "_id": "K7N259JP8I363OMC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Invitation of Chaos", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/clover-luck-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Once per rest, when you succeed on a check, you can choose to fail it instead to gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die. </p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Invite Chaos", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "short", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "95LFWCUJ0S9AQ254", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Rule of All", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/diplomacy-unity-alliance.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Once per long rest, as a reaction, you can send out a burst of unseen chaotic energy at a creature you can see within 60 feet. That creature is struck by a brief confusion that undercuts their composure; mental rhythms stumble, words or orders are flubbed, movements are shaky, and complex actions are misordered, causing the intended Lair or Legendary Action to fail.  In addition, that creature cannot use either until the start of its next turn.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Upon reaching the Growth Level at 11th overall level, you can regain usage of Rule of All by taking a Short Rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Chaos Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Rule of All", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "BSNHEGZSSX19MKJ5", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mantra: Sheer Chaos", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/gaming/dice-pair-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you learn this ability, you learn the Mantra <em>Sheer Chaos</em> associated with your <strong>Chaos Number</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Sheer Chaos: </strong>Roll on the 1d100 <em>Sheer Chaos Table</em>, this effect activates at the beginning of your next turn.&nbsp; You can feel this effect building, know what it will be, and can warn your allies.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>While any of your Sheer Chaos effects are active or set to activate on your next turn, you cannot roll again on the <em>Sheer Chaos Table</em>.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Sheer Chaos Table</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td style=\"min-width: 44px;\"><p><strong><em>#</em></strong></p></td><td><p><strong><em>Effect</em></strong></p></td><td style=\"min-width: 44px;\"><p><strong><em>#</em></strong></p></td><td><p><strong><em>Effect</em></strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>1</strong></p></td><td><p>Lose all @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Dice.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>44</strong></p></td><td><p>You are able to speak with animals and understand their speech for 1 minute.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>2</strong></p></td><td><p>You are <strong>silenced</strong> until you end your turn.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>45</strong></p></td><td><p>You have the <em>Force of Will</em> spell active for 1 minute without concentration.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>3</strong></p></td><td><p>On heads, you are <strong>sickened</strong> until you end your turn.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>46</strong></p></td><td><p>You are teleported to a location you can see within 100 feet.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>4-8</strong></p></td><td><p>Roll a 1d6 on the table below and pick one of the options from that.&nbsp; All creatures within 50 feet gain vulnerability to the chosen damage type for 1 minute.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ol><li>Pick: Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing</li><li>Pick: Acid or Poison</li><li>Pick: Chaos or Psychic</li><li>Pick: Cold or Fire</li><li>Pick: Lightning or Force</li><li>Pick: Necrotic or Radiant</li></ol><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>47-49</strong></p></td><td><p>You summon a creature of a CR of half your overall level or lower decided by the GM.&nbsp; It has its own free will, and gains an Intelligence of at least 10 and the ability to speak your language if it lacked these before.&nbsp; While confused by its new locale, the creature initially regards you as an ally and will generally listen to your commands so long as you prove yourself an ally to it.&nbsp; It remains summoned until its hit points reach zero or a separate creature is summoned by Sheer Chaos.&nbsp; This creature&rsquo;s summoning does not prevent you from rolling again on the Sheer Chaos table.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>9-10</strong></p></td><td><p>You are transformed into a Toad as if transformed by the <em>Verminize</em> spell until the end of your next turn.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>50</strong></p></td><td><p>You gain true sight for 1 minute.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>11</strong></p></td><td><p>You are <strong>stunned </strong>until the start of your next turn.</p><p>Gain two @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Dice.</p></td><td><p><strong>51-52</strong></p></td><td><p>Restore all @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Dice.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>12-13</strong></p></td><td><p>Flip a coin.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>On heads, you grow 1 size and your physical attacks are one die size larger.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>On tails, you shrink 1 size, your physical attacks are one die size smaller, and you gain 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Either way, it lasts until the end of your next turn.</p></td><td><p><strong>53-56</strong></p></td><td><p>Pick an object or creature within 60 feet.&nbsp; You suddenly know one detail, secret, or part of its history, as decided by the GM.&nbsp; These facts are presented as if rolling highly on an Intelligence (Culture) check or divining some long-hidden past about the object.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>14</strong></p></td><td><p>You and all adjacent creatures start <strong>bleeding</strong>.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>57</strong></p></td><td><p>You gain the effects of the <strong>Quicken</strong> spell.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>15</strong></p></td><td><p>For the next minute, when you target a creature with a spell, heal all adjacent creatures by 1d6 hp.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>58</strong></p></td><td><p>Gain an additional action on your next turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>16-17</strong></p></td><td><p>You become spiritually linked with the first creature you see for 1 minute.&nbsp; You are both <strong>charmed</strong> by each other, and when either of you take damage, the other takes the same amount of damage.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>59</strong></p></td><td><p>Gain an additional minor action on your next turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>18-20</strong></p></td><td><p>You explode in Chaotic energy, taking 1d4 Chaos damage per Cleric level you have taken, and dealing 1d6 damage per Cleric level to all creatures within 10 feet.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die for each injured ally.</p></td><td><p><strong>60-61</strong></p></td><td><p>You briefly grow surreal ever-changing limbs out of your back that are difficult to describe, and gain a Fly and Swim speed of 100ft until the end of your next turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>21-22</strong></p></td><td><p>An Incept is summoned adjacent to your position.&nbsp; It is hostile to you.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>62</strong></p></td><td><p>Gain an additional reaction on your next turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>23-24</strong></p></td><td><p>Cast <em>Lash Out</em>.&nbsp; Treat yourself as a target for the spell as well.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>63-64</strong></p></td><td><p>You appear identical to another creature of your choice that you have met.&nbsp; This is an illusion that instantly is recognizable as an illusion when someone or something attempts to touch the illusive parts.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>25</strong></p></td><td><p>You are <strong>blinded </strong>until the end of your turn.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>65-67</strong></p></td><td><p>A surreal swirling of energy encapsulates you.&nbsp; You are resistant to all damage types until the start of your next turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>26</strong></p></td><td><p>You are <strong>deafened </strong>until the start of your next turn.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>68</strong></p></td><td><p>Pick a creature within 60 feet, they must roll a DC 13 Presence (Save) check or else become <strong>stunned</strong> until the end of their next turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>27-28</strong></p></td><td><p>The nearest creature to you must make a DC 10 Presence (Save) check.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>On success, nothing happens.</p><p>On failure, you and the nearest creature swap bodies for 1 minute.&nbsp; During this time, your mental attributes remain the same, and whichever of you is a Chaos Cleric gains 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>69-71</strong></p></td><td><p>A duplicate of yourself appears next to you for 1 minute.&nbsp; You and your duplicate are the same person in two bodies, and share all mental faculties, stats, and a turn.&nbsp; Each self can take their own action each turn, but all other actions are shared, movement is split between each self, and your health and mana pool is shared and unchanged.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>29-30</strong></p></td><td><p>If you die within the next 1 minute, your body will be reborn as if affected by the <em>Reincarnate</em> spell 1d4 days later, regardless of whether or not you are alive at that time.&nbsp; When this happens, restore all your @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Dice.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><strong>72-74</strong></p></td><td><p>You can feel your body jitter and jerk, crackling with energy, as if your mana has a mind of its own.&nbsp; All damage you deal becomes Chaos damage until the end of your next turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>31</strong></p></td><td><p>Strange music radiates from you for 1 minute, being audible up to 100 feet away.&nbsp; If your GM is playing music, they must change the song to another song for all to hear.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>75-77</strong></p></td><td><p>The ground around you shifts and twists strangely in a radius of 30 feet, becoming difficult terrain.&nbsp; All other creatures in this radius must make a DC 15 Strength (Save) or Dexterity (Save) check or be Restrained.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>32-33</strong></p></td><td><p>All creatures within 60 feet see strange scintillating shapes that cover parts of their vision, giving disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks and a -5 to Awareness for 1 minute.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>78-80</strong></p></td><td><p>You have +5 AC until the end of your next turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>34-35</strong></p></td><td><p>Flip a coin.</p><p>On heads, you are <strong>frightened</strong> of the largest creature within 60ft until the start of your next turn.</p><p>On tails, you are <strong>frightened</strong> of the smallest creature within 60ft until the start of your next turn.</p><p>Either way, gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>81-85</strong></p></td><td><p>Pick a non-living object nearby that is not being worn or held.&nbsp; It becomes entrapped in chaos, jerking and twisting wildly, and dealing 1d20 chaos damage when touched for the next 1 minute.&nbsp; At the end of this duration, it appears as if nothing had happened to it.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>36</strong></p></td><td><p>You are <strong>deafened </strong>until the start of your next turn.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>86-87</strong></p></td><td><p>Pick a creature within 60 feet, they must roll a DC 15 Presence (Save) check or else become transformed into a Toad as if by the <em>Verminize</em> spell until the end of their next turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>37</strong></p></td><td><p>You have -2 AC until the end of your next turn.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>88</strong></p></td><td><p>You gain the effects of the <strong>Haste</strong> spell.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>38</strong></p></td><td><p>You are <strong>petrified </strong>until the start of your next turn.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>89-90</strong></p></td><td><p>The effects of the <em>Cloak</em> spell are applied to 3 creatures of your choice within 30 feet.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>39</strong></p></td><td><p>You are overwhelmed by vertigo and fall <strong>prone</strong>.</p><p>Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p></td><td><p><strong>91-94</strong></p></td><td><p>Spells cost half mana until the end of your next turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>40</strong></p></td><td><p>You or an adjacent creature of your choice regains 5 hit points at the start of their turn for the next 1 minute.</p></td><td><p><strong>95</strong></p></td><td><p>All creatures within 30 feet must make a DC 15 Presence (Save) check or else become <strong>charmed</strong> by you.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>41</strong></p></td><td><p>All your melee attacks and touch spells inexplicably have a 60ft range for 1 minute.</p></td><td><p><strong>96-98</strong></p></td><td><p>Your form changes as if the spell <em>Mutate</em> was cast on yourself.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>42</strong></p></td><td><p>Become ill-defined and strange in shape, as you take on the essence of another being.&nbsp; For the next 1 minute, when asked to roll a skill check, you can choose any of your skills to make that skill check in.&nbsp; However, you cannot use the same skill twice within the duration.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><strong>99</strong></p></td><td><p>The first Critical Failure you roll, if rolled in the next 1 minute, counts as a Critical Success instead.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>43</strong></p></td><td><p>The area is filled with extremely thick smoke in a radius of 30ft around you.&nbsp; For the duration, anyone within is <strong>blinded</strong> and cannot be seen, and anyone without cannot see creatures within.</p></td><td><p><strong>100</strong></p></td><td><p>A golden apple appears in your hand.&nbsp; Taking a bite from it causes the rest of the apple to disappear, and the creature to roll on this table.&nbsp; Its taste constantly changes in the mouth.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td></tr></tbody></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Chaos Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "JFWE7N4P0B68717F", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Chaos Dominion Spells", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/clover-luck-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Clerics of the Chaos Dominion learn the following spells when able to cast Cleric spells of the same spell level.&nbsp; These spells are always prepared and don&rsquo;t count against your prepared spell amount.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Dominion spells are considered Cleric spells when learned this way.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Chaos Dominion Spells</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Able to Cast</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Spells</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1st Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.7N5KBCOM40ZX65EO]{Arcane Arrows}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.PZLUQ36LJVGLMZ4R]{Lash Out}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2nd Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.A0XHQ6VS7PDGN9FJ]{Cloak}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.FZ8CHP8N6M0PGLI1]{Discombobulate}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3rd Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.VROEDKWBUZ57MFV7]{Rolling Thunder}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.TA1E58P8XATOBEQH]{Virulent Outbreak}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4th Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-4.YL8USCAX1ZTDKOA1]{Shapeshift}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-4.7H0M1UB9Z1ZVHSJ0]{Remove Arms}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5th Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-5.LAT1CHJ5SCDL566O]{Reincarnate}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-5.RS1WH90WHNO7H1AR]{Kinetic Burst}</p></td></tr></tbody></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "V475LKBO4K3Z04IA", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Synchronization of Chaos", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/control/hypnosis-mesmerism-watch.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can spend @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith}&nbsp;Dice in the following ways:</p><ul><li><strong>Synchronization of Chaos:</strong> When multiple creatures are rolling simultaneously for the same reason, including you, you can spend two @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith}&nbsp;Dice to replace another creature&rsquo;s roll result with one of your dice rolls.<br /> Alternatively, when you roll multiple dice at once, you can spend two @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith}&nbsp;Dice to change the result of one die to the result of another die you rolled.&nbsp; <br /> This change cannot trigger an Eikonic Number or Miracle for any creature involved.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Chaos Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "17NZ5JIJ6XJZ18VM", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Thrives in Chaos", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Requirement: </em>The Miracle Adept ability</p><p>Once per long rest, when you skip your turn from taking a Desperate Action in the previous round, trigger a Miracle.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Chaos Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Thrives in Chaos", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "CW7SV7WCSEMZYMHK", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Blade Arms", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/claws/claw-insect-grey.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have two pairs of arms, with the 2nd set located beneath the first.  The forearms of your upper limbs are a pair of sharp chitin blades.  These limbs are considered natural weapons equivalent to shortswords.  You are proficient with these blades, and can use them as if dual-wielding.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You do not gain extra attacks, actions or minor actions with these limbs.  Additionally, while wearing any armor, shields only grant bonuses when held in 2 hands due to limited mobility.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "attribute": "str", "actionType": "mwak", "chatFlavor": "Finesse, Light", "damage": {"parts": [["1d6 + @mod", "piercing"]], "versatile": ""}, "proficient": true, "properties": {"amm": false, "fin": true, "foc": false, "hvy": false, "lgt": true, "lod": false, "rch": false, "spc": false, "thr": false, "two": false, "una": false, "ver": false}, "showInAttacks": true}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "BX78MZPVZ495PPDG", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Death Sting", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/biological/stinger-insect-grey.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have a stinger on your abdomen that is bred to kill. If you attempt to sting a creature with it, make a melee weapon attack with proficiency. On hit, the target takes 1d10 piercing damage, and you take 1d10 chaos damage as the stinger rips out. On a critical hit, the target becomes @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.SRRBLPRSJWGUR551]{Poisoned}. Otherwise the target must make a Constitution (Save) Check of DC 10 + your proficiency bonus. On failure, the creature takes 1d6 poison damage and is @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9X088PM7H5U2S1HQ]{Sickened} until the end of your next turn. <br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You cannot use this racial trait again until you take a <em>Long Rest Action</em> to focus your body on regrowing the stinger.</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.rest-actions.YLOTM7EKMWPAIQ2E]{Regrow Stinger}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 1, "style": "counter", "name": "Death Sting", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "Must use a Long Rest Action to regrow stinger.", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "W2JOTIASQTIRW3IA", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Extra Arms", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/claws/claw-insect-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have two pairs of arms, with the 2nd set located beneath the first.  You can choose either set of arms to complete actions with, can carry or hold things in up to all four hands, can carry up to 2 two-handed objects, and can reload up to 2 loading weapons at once without penalty.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;However, you do not gain extra attacks, actions, or minor actions with these limbs.  If you hold more than two shields, you only gain the Armor Class bonuses of the first two, as more than two becomes unwieldy and unhelpful.  Additionally, while wearing any armor, shields only grant bonuses when held in 2 hands due to limited mobility.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "5QYD3QFDLZO2NKCD", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Flutter Fall", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/biological/wing-insect-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While conscious, you flutter your wings to prevent yourself from taking falling damage.  This does not apply while wearing heavy armor.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "XQVA2ZE3HFJHJ8Z4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Flutter Jump", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/biological/wing-insect-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your fluttering wings add a +10ft to your vertical and horizontal jump distance.  This distance is halved while wearing heavy armor.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "3RN1CJEJ8YBYOC14", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Handsy", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/claws/claw-insect-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Whenever you make a Strength (Athletics) check to grapple a creature of equal or smaller size using all four arms, then you gain advantage.  Once you succeed at grappling a target this way, you cannot gain this benefit again for the next hour.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "ND986T2ORMSDKFYJ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Lifter", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/claws/claw-insect-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You count as one size larger when determining your carrying capacity and the weight you can push, drag, or lift.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "4F8FWF6AU6ZW5AWV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Multitasker", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/claws/claw-insect-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>With your extra hands, you can work with your hands more efficiently than others. <br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;When taking a <em>Long Rest Action</em> to work a trade based on using your hands, you can additionally take a <em>Rest Action</em>, getting more done in less time. <br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;In addition, for each hour spent working with your hands, you complete 1.5 hours of work. For example, an 8 hour task can be completed in 6 hours instead.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "DSW72S4UGRPZ789H", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Natural Armor", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/claws/claw-insect-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your chitin exoskeleton is comparably tough.  While not wearing armor, your Armor Class is 11 + your Dexterity Modifier.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2S9EWQFOXT06P29E", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Olfactory Antennae", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/claws/claw-insect-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Scout chk'tu have highly specialized antennae built for foraging.  By smell alone, they are able to locate and identify flowers and other notably scented flora at up to 100ft away.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "PX53DTW4FKMESH8I", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Royal Piping", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/tools/instruments/megaphone.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As a minor action, you can let loose a loud piping or horn noise like a howl that radiates up to 120ft.  All sleeping creatures that hear it are awoken, and up to 5 allied creatures of your choice that hear it gain temporary hit points equal to 5 or your level, whichever is higher.  Temporary hit points gained this way can be stacked.  You can use this racial ability once per long or short rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Royal Piping", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "short", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "6LMVQ9ZOP41IHVCP", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Acts of Faith", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/holy/prayer-hands-glowing-yellow-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can spend @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice in the following ways.&nbsp; If an ability does not specify a specific amount of @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice, then you can spend up to as many @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice as you have available:</p><ul><li><strong>Divine Cure:</strong> As part of healing a creature, spend your @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice to increase the hit points recovered.&nbsp; Alternatively, touch a creature and spend your @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice to heal it directly as an Action.</li><li><strong>Divine Deflection:</strong> As a Reaction, you can spend @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice to decrease the attack roll of any creature within 30 feet.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Divine Karma:</strong> As a Reaction, before you know the result of the roll, you can spend 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Die to decrease the number rolled on any (Save) check done by any creature within 15 feet.&nbsp; This cannot be stacked.</li><li><strong>Divine Protection:</strong> As a Reaction, spend your @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice to increase the number rolled on any (Save) check done by any creature within 15 feet.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Divine Smite:</strong> As part of an attack action or spell attack that deals damage, you can spend @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice to increase the damage of the attack.&nbsp; If you roll an Eikonic Number as part of the attack roll, deal 5 additional Radiant damage.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Cleric", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "JE4KI8AHSZRG8WHH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Clerical Approach", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-tooled-blue-yellow.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>The world is filled with countless religious and magical denominations and forms of belief.&nbsp; This information is no secret to a cleric, and often their interactions with such differing forms of belief or magic can affect their magics themselves.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>The following is a list of viewpoints on contradictory beliefs.&nbsp; When you take this ability, choose one of the following forms of belief, as well as the trait with it.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>To change your character&rsquo;s form of belief, you must reach a philosophical breakthrough as a <em>Long Rest Action</em>.&nbsp; When you do, you lose access to the trait of your previous Clerical Approach, and may choose another one.&nbsp; This process is mentally taxing, and you cannot make the change again until 1 month after choosing a Clerical Approach.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.rest-actions.QCJ0RCMG5ZDKN597]{Philosophical Breakthrough}</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Exclusivism&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Exclusivist clerics are those that believe that there is only one &ldquo;correct&rdquo; truth or form of belief, and that the beliefs of others are counterfeits or corruptions of the truth.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Trait</em>: When you prepare spells for the day, you can prepare 2 extra spells.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>When damaged by a spell that you have prepared from your cleric spell list, you can spend your reaction to halve the spell&rsquo;s damage to yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inclusivism</strong></p><p>Inclusivists believe that all forms of faith or belief point to a singular truth, encouraged by similarities and downplaying differences between different faiths.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Trait</em>: As an action, you can replicate onto yourself the effects of a concentration spell that you can see affecting another creature within 30ft of you.&nbsp; The effect only lasts until the start of your next turn.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>If the spell is of a higher spell level than you can cast, the initial action costs 2 Mana.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Pluralism</strong></p><p>Pluralists make little distinction between faiths. Each is valid to the particular cultures or groups that follow them.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Trait</em>: When a creature casts a non-concentration spell within 60ft of you, you can replicate the spell once within 1 minute of the spell happening at the Mana cost of 2 + the Mana cost of the spell.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>You cannot replicate 8th or 9th level spells.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Syncretism</strong></p><p>Syncretists carry a unique faith based on their personal life context, believing bits and pieces of numerous different beliefs that best fit their viewpoints and experiences.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Trait</em>: You learn 1 cantrip from any spell list.&nbsp; Additionally, for each spell level that you become able to cast or have been able to cast above 1st, add a non-Cleric spell to your Cleric spell list. These spells can be prepared and count as Cleric spells, and use Wisdom as their spellcasting ability.</p><p>You cannot gain access to non-Cleric spells of 8th or 9th level this way.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "novice"}, "requirements": "Must have the Cleric Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": "", "style": "choice", "name": "Clerical Approach", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "Can be changed as a Long Rest action, but only once per month.", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "clerical-approach", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": ["Exclusivism", "Inclusivism", "Pluralism", "Syncretism"]}}, "folder": null, "_id": "RVBAX8AXLOK0TRYA", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Divine Inspiraiton", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/holy/yin-yang-balance-symbol.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have become well-versed in the mantras and ways of your beliefs.  Seldom are the moments when you are found at a loss for inspiration with your faith to guide you.</p><p>&nbsp;When you roll any of your @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.CTOHXD4403501WIK]{Eikonic Numbers}, you can immediately activate one of the following Mantras.</p><ul><li>Your Awareness and Wisdom (Perception) checks are increased by +5 until the end of your next turn.</li><li>Your AC increases by +1 until the end of your next turn.</li><li>You gain +1 on all save checks until the end of your next turn.</li><li>You can restore up to your Wisdom Modifier worth of temporary hit points distributed amongst creatures within 15 feet of you.</li><li>You have +1 on skill checks until the end of your next turn.</li><li>Any unassigned Mantra from the same Divine Dominion as the rolled Eikonic Number.</li></ul><p><br />&nbsp;Upon reaching the Growth Level at 11th overall level, you can activate this ability twice when you roll an Eikonic Number.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "novice"}, "requirements": "Must have the Cleric Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "8JTZPLSCYX3QARDO", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Eikonic Numbers", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/holy/prayer-hands-glowing-yellow.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Every Cleric has a mark or idea that symbolizes their faith; an Eikon. When you feel this faith manifest, you give your mantras life&mdash;either vocally or internally&mdash;channeling that belief into action.</p><p><strong>Eikonic Numbers and Mantras</strong></p><p><strong>Eikonic Numbers</strong> trigger assigned <strong>Mantra</strong> effects when rolled. Any time you are rolling dice and naturally roll one of your Eikonic Numbers on a die of any size, treating d100 rolls as a single die, you activate all Mantra effects associated with the rolled Eikonic Number. These effects stack, even if you roll your Eikonic Number more than once as part of a single roll. When you roll with Disadvantage, your Eikonic Number only triggers if it matches the lower of the two results.</p><p><strong>Gaining Eikonic Numbers and Mantras</strong></p><p>In general, when you gain an Eikonic Number, you must pick a number from 7 through 12 that isn&rsquo;t already one of your Eikonic Numbers.</p><p>Eikonic Numbers are categorized by potency: Lesser (7 or 8), Moderate (9 or 10), or Greater (11 or 12). Eikonic Number Potency determines how many <strong>Mantras</strong> can be assigned to it, and is based on how often that number gets rolled. Lower potency numbers are rolled more frequently (fewer dice can roll the higher potency numbers) but trigger fewer Mantras, while higher potencies are less frequent but trigger multiple Mantras simultaneously.</p><p>Mantras can only be assigned to their associated Eikonic Number, up to the number&rsquo;s <em>Mantra Limit</em> as defined by its Potency in table below. You can replace assigned mantras when you gain a level in Cleric or on a Growth level.</p><p>If you have multiple Cleric sub-classes, you can gain more Eikonic Numbers by choosing to take the &ldquo;Eikon&rdquo; ability from subsequent sub-classes.</p><p><em>Eikonic Number Potency Table</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Potency</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Available Eikonic Numbers</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Mantra Limit</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Lesser</p></td><td><p>7 or 8</p></td><td><p>1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Moderate</p></td><td><p>9 or 10</p></td><td><p>2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Greater</p></td><td><p>11 or 12</p></td><td><p>2, plus Faith Abides*</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>* When you roll a Greater Potency Eikonic Number, Faith Abides (from the Faith ability) also activates without having to replace a Mantra effect.</em></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Cleric", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "CTOHXD4403501WIK", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Faith", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/holy/prayer-hands-glowing-yellow.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>At their core, a Cleric is one whose faith gets them through tough situations.  A Cleric without faith is no Cleric at all.<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice are <strong>1d6s</strong> that can be spent on various Cleric abilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You can retain up to 2 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice by default.&nbsp; That maximum increases for every odd-numbered Cleric level gained starting at Cleric level 3.&nbsp; For example, at Cleric level 8, you can hold a maximum of 5 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Die on a long rest. If you gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Die while at your maximum, roll the @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Die and gain temporary hit points equal to the result.&nbsp; If you lose a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Die while out of @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice, unless stated otherwise, your @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice goes into the negative.&nbsp; There is no negative cap to @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice.&nbsp; While you have negative amounts of @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice, you cannot use abilities that cost @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice, and you have Disadvantage on Wisdom (Save) and Wisdom (Theology) checks.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You cannot trigger your Eikonic Number, a Natural 1, or a Natural 20 via the spending of your @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{Faith}&nbsp;Dice.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Additionally, when you roll your Eikonic Number, you can replace one <strong>Mantra</strong> with the following effect:</p><ul><li><em>Faith Abides:</em> Gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Cleric", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Faith (d6)", "valueFrom": "formula", "maxFormula": "ceil(@cleric/2)+1", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "gain", "rechargeFormula": "1", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "Gain 1d6 temporary hit points.", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "65D4NMYRBMKHW59K", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Miracle", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/holy/chalice-glowing-gold-water.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Roll doubles on your @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith}&nbsp;Dice</li><li>Roll doubles of any of your Eikonic Numbers on a d20 roll with advantage</li><li>Roll any of your Eikonic Numbers on a 1d100 roll</li></ul><p>Then you can choose to activate one of the following Miracle options:</p><ul><li><strong>Ex Tempore:</strong> Immediately cast a spell as a Non-Action.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Deus Ex Machina:</strong> Before the end of your next turn, you can cast a Cleric spell of 1 spell level higher than the highest leveled spell that you know.</li><li><strong>Ex Nihilo: </strong>Before your next rest, the next spell you cast costs no Mana if it is of a spell level equal or lower than half your Proficiency Bonus.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Cleric", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "BREZS34CQ6PFBCNF", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Prayer", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/holy/prayer-hands-glowing-yellow-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>During a long rest, you can enter into a communion with your deity or complete a ritual core to your belief.&nbsp; When you do, roll a 1d100.&nbsp; Your result determines which divine effect you will receive until your next long rest or until 24 hours pass, whichever comes first.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>After seeing your result on the <em>Prayer Results Table</em>, you can choose to either increase or reduce the result at the cost of 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith}&nbsp;Die.&nbsp; Once you do,&nbsp; roll the @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith}&nbsp;Die and apply it to the result.&nbsp; If you spend a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith}&nbsp;Die on this, then if the result is less than 1 or greater than 97, change the result to a 1.&nbsp; You cannot spend more than 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith}&nbsp;Die per rest in this way.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Prayer Result Table</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td style=\"min-width:50px;\"><p><strong>Faith Roll Result</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Effect</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>01</p></td><td><p>You are filled with doubt.&nbsp; Your @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith} Dice are set to -1 and you cannot gain @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith} Dice.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>02-20</p></td><td><p>No response.&nbsp; No effect.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>21-40</p></td><td><p>Select one Cleric Mantra. You can activate that Mantra as a non-action once.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>41-42</p></td><td><p>Your awareness increases by +5.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>43-44</p></td><td><p>When you speak, all creatures understand what you are saying.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>45-46</p></td><td><p>You have advantage on Intelligence (Save), Wisdom (Save), and Presence (Save) checks.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>46-47</p></td><td><p>You can trigger a Cleric Miracle as a non-action once.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>48-51</p></td><td><p>You have a hover flying speed of 60 feet.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>52-53</p></td><td><p>You can see @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.YE63H7VLOHW7NFHO]{Invisible} creatures.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>54-57</p></td><td><p>You have advantage on one d20 roll of your choice.&nbsp; You can choose to apply this to a roll after seeing the result.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>58-62</p></td><td><p>Your AC increases by 1.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>63-69</p></td><td><p>You are immune to becoming @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9YPWLY1IHQV3MRLO]{Diseased}, @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.SRRBLPRSJWGUR551]{Poisoned} (including inebriation), @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9X088PM7H5U2S1HQ]{Sickened}, and @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed}.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>70-74</p></td><td><p>When you land an attack, you are healed by 1d4 Hit Points.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>75-77</p></td><td><p>You gain 5 times your proficiency bonus in temporary Hit Points.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>78-82</p></td><td><p>As an action, you can spend any number of your Hit Dice to heal creatures within touch.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>83-85</p></td><td><p>You can transform yourself into and out of any form option available for <strong>Shapeshift</strong> as a minor action.&nbsp; These forms all follow the rules of the Shapeshift spell, except they have a share Hit Point pool equal to double your overall level that is retained between transformations. When this pool of Hit Points falls to 0, you are transformed back, you subtract the maximum Hit Points of the form from your normal current Hit Points, and this Prayer Result is no longer.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>86-88</p></td><td><p>If a creature touches you or anything on your person, it regains 1d10 Hit Points and is cured of @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9YPWLY1IHQV3MRLO]{Disease}.&nbsp; In addition, the creature must make a Wisdom (Save) check against your spell save DC or be @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed} by you for 1 minute.&nbsp; The creature repeats this save at the beginning of each turn until it passes and the charm is removed.&nbsp; Once a creature has been affected by this once, it cannot be affected again.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>89-90</p></td><td><p>Gain Immunity to one damage type or condition of your choice.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>91-92</p></td><td><p>You gain 1 point of Luck.&nbsp; This does not expire.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>93-94</p></td><td><p>You have 10 more Mana than your maximum. Gain 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith} Die, regardless of your maximum.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>95-96</p></td><td><p>If you die during the duration, you immediately come back to life with full Hit Points one time.&nbsp; If your body is completely destroyed by the attack, you are reborn in a new body as if the spell <strong>Resurrection</strong> was cast on you.&nbsp; Gain 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith} Die, regardless of your maximum.&nbsp; Once this happens, it cannot happen again for the next 24 hours.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>97-99</p></td><td><p>Your belief deepens.&nbsp; Roll twice more on this table and take both results.&nbsp; Reroll results of 01 and 97-99.&nbsp; Gain 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith} Die, regardless of your maximum.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>100</p></td><td><p>You have a profound spiritual experience.&nbsp; You can enter and exit a <strong>Divine Form</strong> as a minor action for the duration.&nbsp; This form retains your general shape and size, but can appear as anything to your liking, so long as it is both fitting to your Dominion and fittingly divine in appearance.&nbsp; All changes and additions are real during this time, but do not add to your capabilities.&nbsp; While in your Divine Form, you have an extra Action, Minor Action, and Reaction per turn, and can Levitate with a Fly Speed of 30ft.&nbsp; Gain 3 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith} Dice, regardless of your maximum.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "adept"}, "requirements": "6th level overall and 3rd level Cleric", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "ASZ0LJ8H48GD7DQ6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Providence", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/nature/cornucopia-orange.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When preparing spells as a part of a rest, you can select a creature nearby, one of your Eikonic Numbers, and one Mantra you know, so long as the Mantra can be associated with that Eikonic Number.  Until your next long rest, when that creature rolls the selected Eikonic Number, they gain the benefit of the selected Mantra and you gain 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.  Once per long rest, if they fall unconscious, you can activate a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.BREZS34CQ6PFBCNF]{Miracle}.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "adept"}, "requirements": "6th level overall and 3rd level Cleric", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Providence", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "JWUZ8MK65EG4I4MB", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Self-Sacrifice", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-stack.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Should you take damage from <strong>Saving a Target</strong> as a desperate action, the following happens:</p><ul><li>You can spend 1 of your Rest Dice to restore your Hit Points.</li><li>You can spend 1 of your Rest Dice to restore the saved target&rsquo;s Hit Points.</li><li>Gain 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&amp;#x1F56F; Faith}&nbsp;Die.</li><li>If the saved target would have fallen <strong>unconscious </strong>before you intervened, you can make an opportunity attack against the attacker as a non-action.</li><li>If you fall <strong>unconscious</strong> from the attack, the saved target regains Hit Points up to half of the damage dealt to you.</li><li>If you are <strong>Killed Instantly</strong>, the protected creature learns one of your Mantras permanently assigned to the Eikonic Number that you had it assigned to. They know this Mantra so long as you are dead.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Must have a Cleric Adept Ability", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "9QL8V9MDFLPW6JTH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spellcasting (Cleric)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/rune-sigil-black-pink.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your connection to your deity has been rewarded with the miracle of spellcasting.  Despite your previous capabilities at spellcasting, you find yourself progressively more magically capable by channeling your natural Mana through your faith in your deity.</p><h4><strong>Cantrips</strong></h4><p>Upon gaining your 1st level of Cleric, you know three Cantrips from the Cleric's spell list.  You will learn additional cantrips as you advance in the Cleric class.  You gain an additional Cantrip when you hit Adept Cleric, and then another at Expert Cleric.</p><h4><strong>Preparing and Casting Spells</strong></h4><p>A Cleric, like all spellcasters, expends Mana to cast spells (expanded upon in the Mana section of Magic).&nbsp; As well, you regain your Mana fully on a long rest, and partially on a short rest.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Like other spellcasters, a Cleric can prepare and memorize a list of spells that they can cast each day.&nbsp; However, since Clerics lean upon their deities for their magic, they do not learn Cleric spells in the traditional sense.&nbsp; Instead, they become capable enough to channel more powerful spells.&nbsp; As such, Clerics can prepare a number of spells from the Cleric spell list that they are capable of casting equal to:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Your Cleric level + your Wisdom modifier, (minimum of 1)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>These are the spells that can be chosen from this day.&nbsp; For example, Thadius is a 5th level Cleric with a Wisdom of 17.&nbsp; He can prepare eight spells, picking a combination of spells from the 1st, 2nd, or 3rd level Cleric spell.&nbsp; Thadius can cast any spell he wants until he runs out of Mana, but he cannot cast a spell that he has not prepared.&nbsp; This means that if he has 2 Mana left, but has only prepared 3rd level spells, then the Mana will go unused until he regains Mana or prepares new spells.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A Cleric can change the spells they have prepared at the end of any long rest they take.&nbsp; The act of preparing them does take time, though.&nbsp; It takes 1 minute per spell level for each spell on your list of prepared spells.</p><h4><strong>Spellcasting Ability</strong></h4><p>Being that you obtain your magic ability through intense devotion and faith, Wisdom is the spellcasting ability for a Cleric.  Meaning that your Wisdom modifier comes into play when setting the DC for your Cleric spells and when making an attack with one.</p><ul><li><i>Spell Save DC:</i> 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier</li><li><i>Spell Attack Modifier:</i> your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier</li></ul><h4><strong>Ritual Casting</strong></h4><p>You can cast a Cleric spell as a ritual if that spell has the Ritual tag, and you have the spell prepared.</p><h4><strong>Holy Spellcasting Focus</strong></h4><p>You may use a holy focus, a specialized item used to channel and cast spells, as a spellcasting focus for casting your Cleric spells.<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;While in the Cleric's possession, a spellcasting focus allows spells to be cast without most material components.  Material components that have a cost or are said to be used up by the spell cannot be replaced using an arcane focus.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Cleric", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "SWRVTEHG4DXWU4VK", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Cleric Spells", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-runed-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>1st level Clerics get access to Cleric Spells, which consists of 1st through 7th level spells.  However, you do not have access to all of them right away.  These spell levels become accessible as follows:</p><p><i>Cleric Spell Levels</i></p><table><tr><th>Spell Level</th><th>Unlock Requirements</th></tr><tr><td>Level 1 Spells</td><td>1st Level Cleric.</td></tr><tr><td>Level 2 Spells</td><td>2nd Level Cleric;<br>3rd Level Overall.</td></tr><tr><td>Level 3 Spells</td><td>3rd Level Cleric;<br>5th Level Overall<br>(At least 4 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 4 Spells</td><td>4th Level Cleric;<br>7th Level Overall<br>(At least 6 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 5 Spells</td><td>5th Level Cleric;<br>9th Level Overall<br>(At least 8 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 6 Spells</td><td>6th Level Cleric;<br>11th Level Overall<br>(At least 10 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 7 Spells</td><td>7th Level Cleric;<br>13th Level Overall<br>(At least 12 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Cleric", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "K1Q6UGY7O0CBB4KD", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Darkvision (30ft)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/perception/eye-tendrils-web-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have superior vision in the dark, and can see in dim light within 30 feet of you as if it were in bright conditions, and can see in darkness as if it were dim conditions up to the same distance.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "K2R4176S4B99TO6R", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Darkvision (60ft)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/perception/eye-tendrils-web-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have superior vision in the dark, and can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were in bright conditions, and can see in darkness as if it were dim conditions up to the same distance.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "1F3VSNLQTVMYA4PE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fey Ancestry", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/consumables/fruit/apple-red-tree-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have advantage on save checks against being @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed}, and magic can't put you to sleep.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "B6D7U0WZJRIXIX5O", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Lesser Fey Ancestry", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/consumables/fruit/apple-red-tree-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have advantage on save checks against magically being put to sleep.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "N3YTNUP9KU47ZSZV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Magic Means Nothing", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/movement/figure-running-gray.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>If you would be reduced to 0 hit points by a magical source, you can choose to instead be at 1.  This ability can only be used once per long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 1, "style": "counter", "name": "Magic Means Nothing", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "B5HHGGP9E3Z81TY8", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Navigator", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/tools/navigation/compass-brass-blue-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You always know the cardinal direction that you are facing.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "OXY335G1JVFPRA6V", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Road Less Traveled", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/wilderness/terrain-river-road-gray.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are unhindered by non-magical rough terrain.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "FLXLXLGUDQ22W74S", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Unstoppable", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/movement/figure-running-gray.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have advantage on rolls against effects that would keep you from moving.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "LZ84NS4W5BKFFEI8", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Desperate Turn", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-sword-slashing-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>When everything falls apart, you have to do more&mdash;it may be your only chance to turn the tide. </em></p><p><br />Once per long rest, as a Desperate Action, immediately take an entire extra turn. At the end of this desperate turn, do not gain the @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.QUP5YUWBCXD17R7E]{Desperate} condition. However, you cannot take a desperate action until the end of your next turn.<br />Like any normal turn, this triggers any &ldquo;on your turn&rdquo; effects.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "adept"}, "requirements": "6th level overall and 3rd level Fighter", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Desperate Turn", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "F0XR725A3FMS2V7I", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Extra Attack", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/strikes-sword-scimitar.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>As combat becomes your constant companion, you learn how to attack twice as quickly without sacrificing power. </em></p><p>When you make an attack action, you can make two attacks instead of one.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "adept"}, "requirements": "6th level overall and 3rd level Fighter", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "SH5OCGLHHXV66GKI", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fighting Stance", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/people/infantry.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Through experimentation, practice, or mentorship, you have learned new methods of battle. Fighting Stances each introduce their own benefits and deficits, but only while in use. Knowing when to enter or exit them is key to a successful battle. </em></p><p>You know 2 Fighting Stances from the Stance List below. So long as you meet a known stance&rsquo;s requirements, you can enter a Fighting Stance either before taking an action on your first turn in combat, after an attack action, or as a minor action.</p><p>You automatically exit and are unable to enter Fighting Stances while you do not meet the stance&rsquo;s requirements, are @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.RK3DF56CKMQUV6DM]{Prone}, @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.PEDR1J13VZXKUF3C]{Stunned}, or @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9KB959MRZ0H4IT4C]{Unconscious}, or sheathe, drop, or lose possession of the weapon required by the stance. If you exit a stance instead of swapping to another, you retain the stance&rsquo;s <em>Cons</em> until the start of your next turn. <br />If a stance requires a weapon trait, all wielded weapons must share that trait. Shields and natural weapons do not count against this, but they also do not gain the stance&rsquo;s <em>Pros</em> unless they also have the weapon trait(s) required by the stance.</p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Learning New Stances</strong>: You learn 2 more stances at each Growth Level.<br />Martial Archetypes typically have expanded Fighting Stance options that either become immediately available, or are added to the list of stances you can learn at each Growth Level.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><br><br><p><u><i>Stance List</i></u><br>@Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.AQKR36ORJ8UW7M7O]{Ammunition Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.U0YH0GDRUF7KZ3HP]{Boxing Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.59STQWZ34C00OVZP]{Finesse Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.4RWGBRI6CNCPMKCG]{Heavy Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.QEDI2ZY7AFB0GFXY]{Light Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.7ECXODBQJAZNTQFS]{Loading Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.TO8A2T5QL9GR8MAF]{One-Handed Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.98PGZKRSGDG2L2L7]{Quick-Draw Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.SK2FZU8XH2UZX0GP]{Ranged Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.H2554TR82JFKPYS2]{Reach Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.5TS3VRP8JKUPXU0Z]{Shield Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.4IQUGM1GK28XR39P]{Slugger Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.XK4PEQX6RYXIKTZ6]{Throwing Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.CAIFAC3V8NQRCZUQ]{Two-Handed Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.fighting-stances.OV4KEWGS7DFIDZ0Q]{Versatile Stance}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Fighter", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": "", "style": "choice", "name": "Fighting Stance", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "none", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "fighting-stance", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "8O5S8E5F8E9ZQ5MP", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Size Up", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/control/silhouette-grow-shrink-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can size up a living creature that you can see as a non-action. When you do so, the GM tells you if the creature&rsquo;s hit points are:</p><ul><li>Zero</li><li>Less than &frac14;</li><li>Less than &frac12;</li><li>Less than &frac34;</li><li>Less than full</li><li>Full</li><li>Greater than full</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Fighter", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "92GYIVKSFZIMYTB4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Strike Down", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-axe-blood-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Fighting requires more precision than some think. Less than an inch is the difference between a vital organ or a flesh wound. Fighters know that finishing what you&rsquo;ve started takes numbers off the field, and when an opponent is low, it&rsquo;s important to finish them off before they have the chance to punish your mistake. </em></p><p>As a reaction after injuring a creature on your turn, if the creature has less than &frac14; hit points remaining, then the creature takes additional chaos damage equal to your overall level.</p><p>If this reaction reduces the creature to 0 hit points, you can take an additional Action this turn.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "novice"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "S8VA8DQKIDWB6127", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Thrives Under Pressure", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/hand-grip-staff-teal.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>At any point during a Desperate Action, you can do all of the following as non-actions:</p><ul><li>Swap weapons, even heavy weapons.</li><li>Swap, enter, or exit your Fighting Stance.</li><li>Move up to half your movement speed, unslowed by difficult or tight terrain.</li></ul><p>In addition, until the end of your next turn:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>You are proficient with all weapons.</li><li>You have a +2 to all Save Checks.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Must have a Fighter Adept Ability", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "ZBXFQL0LWH9PQUNJ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Weapon Fanatic", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/swords-triple-orange.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>For each growth level, gain proficiency in 2 more weapons. This also applies for all previously obtained growth levels.</p><p>Additionally, you have advantage on all Intelligence (Culture) and Intelligence (Investigation) checks related to weapons or armors with which you are proficient, or Fighting Stances in which you know.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Must have a Fighter Adept Ability", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "57K1WUK53JJUHQ6N", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Weapon Savvy", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-weapons-orange.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>All warriors have their weapons of choice. While most adventurers rely on general proficiency to survive, you refused to stop there. With enough practice, you&rsquo;ve begun to unlock your weapon&rsquo;s hidden potential. </em></p><p>Fighters who become savvy with a weapon gain bonuses that surpass proficiency and open new ways to wield that type of weapon.</p><p>Pick three weapons with which you are already proficient. You become <em>Savvy</em> with these weapons. So long as you are wielding a savvy weapon, you gain the relevant weapon effects from the table below. In addition, you gain a +1 to Attack Rolls with your Savvy weapons.</p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Learning New Savvies</strong>: You learn 1 additional savvy at each Growth Level.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><br /><br /><br /><br /></p><p><strong><em>Savvy Effects: </em></strong>While using the weapon of choice that you are Savvy with, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><em>Savvy Effect Table</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td style='min-width: 100px;'><p><strong>Weapon</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Effect</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Axes </strong>(Hatchets, Battleaxes, or Greataxes)</p></td><td><p><em>Guillotine Strike (Passive)</em>: Your attacks deal 1d12 extra damage to @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.RK3DF56CKMQUV6DM]{Prone} creatures. If the attack kills a humanoid, it can behead the creature.</p><br /><p><em>Deforestation (Passive)</em>: Your attacks deal an additional 1d8 slashing damage to plants. Additionally, wooden objects and structures take double damage from your attacks.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Blowgun</strong></p></td><td><p><em>First Strike (Passive):</em> Attacks made with this weapon while hidden are made at Advantage.</p><br /><p><em>Tranquilizer (Passive):</em> Attacks with this weapon deal an additional 1d6 poison damage, and the creature must make a Constitution (Save) check against a DC of 15 or be @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9X088PM7H5U2S1HQ]{Sickened} for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Bludgeons </strong>(Clubs, Greatclubs, Hammers, or Knuckles)</p></td><td><p><em>Concussion (Passive)</em>: When you land a critical hit, you can instead choose to forgo the extra critical hit damage in order to apply the @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.PEDR1J13VZXKUF3C]{Stunned} condition to the target until the end of its next turn.</p><br /><p><em>Bell Ringer (Minor Action)</em>: As a minor action, your next attack with this weapon this turn causes the target to also make a Constitution (Save) check of DC 10 + Strength Modifier, causing the target to be @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.LM1J0T2XZ0KS1UFK]{Muddled} and @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.3BAHKVP3ZKFC7BJD]{Staggered} on failure until the end of its turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Bows </strong>(Shortbows or Longbows)</p></td><td><p><em>Suppression (Action):</em> As an action, you can expend 5 ammunition to suppress all targets within a 15ft cone until your next turn with a flurry of shots in the area. Suppressed targets get disadvantage on attack rolls while in the area, and if they move while under suppression then you can use your reaction to make an opportunity attack against them. If you take a desperate action before your next turn then suppression ends.</p><br /><p><em>Arrow Curving (Passive)</em>: Your attack rolls are unaffected by half-cover, three-quarters cover, or the target being @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.RK3DF56CKMQUV6DM]{Prone}.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Crossbows </strong>(Light, Hand, Heavy, or Repeating Crossbows)</p></td><td><p><em>Stock Bash (Minor Action):</em> Your crossbow can be used as a 1d4 bludgeoning melee weapon as a minor action. If you hit a creature with this melee attack, you automatically Disengage from that target and have advantage on attacking them with your crossbow on this turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Dagger</strong></p></td><td><p><em>Slit the Throat (Passive)</em>: You deal 1d10 extra damage to @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FGVFFYGPAFQGZ5RP]{Grappled}, @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.3CQC3JEY2C3Y721F]{Incapacitated}, or @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.1EK5V6KTYAWC6S69]{Restrained} creatures.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Dart</strong></p></td><td><p><em>Pinpoint (Passive)</em>: Your proficiency bonus is doubled for attack rolls with this weapon.</p><br /><p><em>Anchoring Shot (Minor Action): </em>As a minor action, your next dart attack this turn becomes an Anchoring Shot. If this attack hits a flying, swimming, or riding creature, then the target must make a Dexterity (Save) check of DC 10 + your Strength Modifier.</p><p>On failure:</p><ul><li>The flying creature falls 10ft and repeats the check until it hits something or succeeds the save.</li><li>The swimming creature falls 10ft.</li><li>The riding creature is dismounted and falls @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.RK3DF56CKMQUV6DM]{Prone}.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Hooked Blades</strong> (Scythe or Sickle)</p></td><td><p><em>Reap (Attack)</em>: Once per turn in place of an attack, you can attack two creatures within reach and within 5ft of each other.</p><br /><p><em>Sow (Minor Action):</em> As a minor action, you wind your weapon back to prepare to reap. The next time you use <em>Reap</em> this turn, you can target any two creatures within reach.</p><br /><p><em>Nick (Passive):</em> When you miss an attack, deal 1 slashing damage to the target.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Maces </strong>(Maces or Flails)</p></td><td><p><em>Internal Injury (Passive):</em> When you attack a @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.RK3DF56CKMQUV6DM]{Prone} creature, it takes an extra 1d6 bludgeoning damage and it must make a Constitution (Save) check of DC 8 + your Strength modifier. On failure, the creature takes 1d6 extra chaos damage at the beginning of its next turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Morning Star</strong></p></td><td><p><em>Aerate (Passive)</em>: When you land an attack, the target must make a Constitution (Save) check of DC 8 + your attack modifier. On failure, the creature gains 2 @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.R54LQEKSDXNQ3N75]{Bleeding}.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Pickaxe</strong></p></td><td><p><em>Pierce (Passive)</em>: When targeting creatures with natural armor or wearing armor, add an amount equal to your proficiency bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls. This bonus is added after normal proficiency bonuses are added.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Pike</strong></p></td><td><p><em>Hold Position (Reaction)</em>: While in Self-Defense, you can use your reaction to make an opportunity attack on a creature that moves into or within your attack range. If the attack hits, you regain your reaction and Hold Position ends.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Polearms </strong>(Glaive or Lance)</p></td><td><p><em>Vault (Minor Action): </em>As a minor action, you can plant and push off of your weapon to launch yourself higher, increasing your jump height or distance by +10ft.</p><br /><p><em>Riding Weapons (Passive)</em>: Attacks against non-mounted creatures while on a mount have a +3 to hit, and deal an additional 1d6 force damage.</p><br /><p><em>Anti-Riding Weapons (Passive)</em>: Attacks against mounted creatures are made at advantage.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Quarterstaff</strong></p></td><td><p><em>Sweep the Leg (Minor Action)</em>: As a minor action, take the Trip action.</p><br /><p><em>Follow Down (Reaction)</em>: When a creature within weapon range falls @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.RK3DF56CKMQUV6DM]{Prone}, you can make an opportunity attack against them.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Rapier</strong></p></td><td><p><em>Have At Thee! (Desperate Action):</em> If you use a desperate action before your first turn in combat, you can both move and make an attack action. The first attack made this way deals 3d4 extra piercing damage.</p><br /><p><em>Lunge (Passive):</em> You can add 5ft of range to one attack per turn.</p><br /><p><em>Feint Retreat (Passive)</em>: You can disengage as a non-action after landing an attack on a target.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Shields, One-Handed</strong> (Shields or Bucklers)</p></td><td><p><em>Uncanny Block (Desperate Action)</em>: When a creature that you can see hits you with an attack, you can use a desperate action to reduce the attack&rsquo;s damage against you by half.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Shields, Two-Handed</strong> (Tower Shields)</p></td><td><p><em>Iron Wall (Desperate Action):</em> When you make a Dexterity (Save) check to take half or full damage, you can use your desperate action to protect yourself. If you are holding your shield in two hands, then you can also protect one other creature within 5ft of you. Protected creatures take half damage when they would take full damage, and take no damage if they would take half damage.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Slings </strong>(Slings or Slingshots)</p></td><td><p><em>Cluster Shot (Attack)</em>: In place of an attack, you can attack a single target twice at disadvantage.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Spears </strong>(Javelins, Spears, or Tridents)</p></td><td><p><em>Pierce Pin (Minor Action)</em>: As a minor action, the target of your next attack with this weapon this turn must make a Dexterity (Save) check of DC 8 + your Dexterity Modifier on hit. On failure, they become @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FGVFFYGPAFQGZ5RP]{Grappled} until the end of their next turn as some part of them is pinned to the environment. On success, they become @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.3BAHKVP3ZKFC7BJD]{Staggered} instead. If the target is adjacent to a wall or static object on the opposite side of them from your attack, the save DC increases by +5. Large or larger creatures become staggered on failure and gain no condition on success.</p><br /><p><em>Water Weapon (Passive)</em>: Attack and damage rolls are not negatively affected by being used in or under water.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Swords </strong>(Shortswords, Midswords, Greatswords, or Scimitars)</p></td><td><p><em>Lock Weapons (Passive):</em> When you miss with a melee weapon attack against a creature of equal size who is wielding a weapon or staff, you can attempt to lock weapons with that target. The target must make a Strength (Save) against DC 8 + your Proficiency Bonus + your Strength Modifier. On failure, you two lock your weapons together. While weapon locked, you are both @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.3BAHKVP3ZKFC7BJD]{Staggered}, and your locked weapons are unusable for anything other than making attacks against each other. <br />If either of you ends the weapon lock, then the other can make an opportunity attack against them. The following will end a weapon lock:</p><ul><li>Taking an action other than attacking each other.</li><li>Leaving melee range of each other.</li><li>Choosing to drop the weapon lock as a non-action.</li></ul><br /><p><em>Anbinden (Action):</em> As an action, attack and purposefully miss the target, such that you can activate <em>Lock Weapons</em>.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Throwing Star</strong></p></td><td><p><em>Silent Killer (Passive)</em>: While hidden, attacks with this weapon deal an additional 1d8 damage and the result of your previous Dexterity (Stealth) roll decreases by -2. This may reveal your location if your stealth becomes lower than a creature&rsquo;s Awareness.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Unarmed</strong></p></td><td><p><em>Pushy (Minor Action):</em> As a minor action, take the <strong>shove</strong> action.</p><br /><p><em>Environmental Takedown (Passive)</em>: When you succeed on a <strong>shove</strong> action, pick one structure or other creature within 5ft of you to shove the creature into. Depending on the target, you get one of the following results:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Structure: You smash the creature into a wall, large object, or structure. The creature takes bludgeoning damage equal to your unarmed attack damage. The structure takes equal damage.</li><li>Creature: You grab and slam one creature into another, giving both creatures bludgeoning damage equal to your Strength Modifier.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>War Hammers</strong> (Mauls or Warhammers)</p></td><td><p><em>Ground Slam (Minor Action)</em>: As a minor action, all creatures within 5ft of you must make a Dexterity (Save) check of DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength Modifier. On failure, the creature falls @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.RK3DF56CKMQUV6DM]{Prone}.</p><br /><p><em>Deconstruct (Passive)</em>: Your attacks deal an additional 1d10 bludgeoning damage to constructs. Attacks do double damage to structures and stone objects.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Whips </strong>(Whips or Chain Whips)</p></td><td><p><em>Seize (Reaction)</em>: You can attempt to @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FGVFFYGPAFQGZ5RP]{Grappled} targets in place of your opportunity attack. Grapples made in this way add your proficiency bonus to the result of the grapple check, on top of any Strength (Athletics) bonus.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>&nbsp;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "novice"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "D5L8X9UJQABN9SJA", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Brand-Builder", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Brand Loyalty</em></p><p>Instead of 1 minute, you now keep your current heat for 1 hour of not gaining heat.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Dramatic Entrance</em></p><p>When you roll initiative, your current heat increases by half of your maximum heat.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Pressure to Perform</em></p><p>When making a skill check, you can add +1 to your roll for every 4 heat you spend, up to +5.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "C3FOXDT9CHAKP733", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Crowd-Worker", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Work the Crowd</em></p><p>As a minor action, if at least 1 non-combatant that you can see is watching you fight, you can play to the crowd to gain heat equal to your Presence (Perform) modifier, minimum of 1.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>This is for You</em></p><p>If at least 1 non-combatant that you can see is watching you fight, you can dedicate your next attack.&nbsp; If this attack kills or knocks a creature @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9KB959MRZ0H4IT4C]{Unconscious}, you automatically use &ldquo;Work the Crowd&rdquo; as a non-action.&nbsp; If you do, you can spend your heat to regain Hit Points.&nbsp; For every 1 heat you spend, you gain 1 Hit Point to a maximum of 20.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the attack fails to knock the creature @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9KB959MRZ0H4IT4C]{Unconscious}, you cannot use &ldquo;This is for You&rdquo; again for the next 1 minute.&nbsp; If the attack misses, you lose 10 heat.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "FBB0R61OTQY8CJ45", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Gladiatorial Role", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Gladiators fall into specific roles based on their external image that defines how they perform in different environments.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;When you get this ability, pick one of the following Gladiatorial Roles and gain all of the abilities listed with it.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You can change your Gladiatorial Role, but it takes some time to change your public image and get used to the role.&nbsp; You can do so by practicing your new image as a <em>Long Rest Action</em>.&nbsp; When you do, you lose access to the traits of your previous Gladiatorial Role and may choose another one.&nbsp; If you change Gladiatorial Roles within 1 month of the last change, then you can only gain half heat for 1 week following.</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.rest-actions.QS58G9QJAIP20Y4S]{Heel or Face Turn}</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Gladiatorial Roles</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Gladiatorial Role: Face</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Some gladiators, known as faces, find their fighting energy from being the protagonist.&nbsp; Be it as a hero, a helper, or an entertainer, faces feed off of encouragement.&nbsp; The more that onlookers want faces to win, the more that faces push themselves up to and past their limits.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>You present yourself as an underdog in combat, or otherwise the crowd-demanded overdog, and aim to get people rooting for you to win.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Role Ability: Heat Gain</strong></p><p>When you start your turn, you gain heat equal to half the total damage that you took since the start of your last turn, up to your <strong>Maximum Heat</strong>.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><br /><p><strong>Role Ability: Underdog</strong></p><p>As a minor action, you can gain 1 temporary Hit Point for every 2 heat you spend.&nbsp; This changes to 2 temporary Hit Points for every 2 heat if you have a <strong>Condition</strong>.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>&nbsp;</p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Gladiatorial Role: Heel</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Heels, unlike faces, get their fighting energy from being an antagonist.&nbsp; Jeers drive heels just as much as cheers.&nbsp; No matter the situation, the energy of the room as a whole encourages heels to outshine enemies and allies alike.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>You present yourself as an overdog, antagonist, or menace on the battlefield, aiming for some sort of crowd reaction to drive you past your limits.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Role Ability: Heat Gain</strong></p><p>When you end your turn, you gain heat equal to half the total damage that you dealt this turn, up to your <strong>Maximum Heat</strong>.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><br /><p><strong>Role Ability: Overdog</strong></p><p>Before you make an attack, for every 5 heat you spend, you deal an additional 1d4 damage.&nbsp; This changes to 1d8 additional damage if the target creature has a <strong>Condition</strong>.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "726QUN63DM3JKKPN", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Heat", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>&ldquo;Heat&rdquo; is the cumulative energy that you gain from being witnessed in battle.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>You gain heat based on your Gladiatorial Role, up to your <strong>Maximum Heat</strong>.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Your heat depletes after 1 minute of not gaining heat.</p><p><br /><em>Maximum Heat</em> = 5 times half of your overall level.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Heat", "valueFrom": "formula", "maxFormula": "5*@level", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "short", "rechargeStyle": "set", "rechargeFormula": "0", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "SEFGUA8X0TGZPWT2", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Performer", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain proficiency in Presence (Perform) if you were not already proficient in it.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "0KTT2Y0R01HSBXB3", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fighting Stance: Andabata", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/eyes/humanoid-single-blind.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><i>Requirement:</i> The @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ADW4EH0NKRDCRCA4]{Blinded} condition or some other total lack of sight.</p><hr><p>In some lands, public executions are handled as entertainment, with blindfolded fighting being a popular form.  These prisoners were expected to die in the arena, but some of them continued to survive.  These gladiators had found the secrets to blind fighting, extending their livelihoods in the process.  This strategy did not go unnoticed as word spread of its success, entering more traditional battlefields in the process.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The Andabata Stance is entering a different state of mind.  Instead of fighting for a crowd, those trained in the stance are often after the thrill of fighting blind itself and the risks that brings.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;By widening your stance and obscuring or closing your eyes if not already @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ADW4EH0NKRDCRCA4]{Blinded}, you open your mind and begin to listen.  You feel for vibrations in the ground and sounds in the air, bringing your weapons in close to your body both for defense and to keep from losing them.  With some practice, as your mind clears and focuses, you find yourself able to 'see' without eyes and fight without sight.</p><hr><u>Pros</u><p><b>Blind Thrill</b><ul><li>You gain +10 heat at the beginning of your turn.</li><li>You gain an additional +10 heat if you were attacked this turn, whether it hits or misses.</li></ul><b>Heat Vision</b><ul><li>At the beginning of your turn, you can spend heat to give yourself blindsight as a non-action.  For every 5 heat you spend you have 5ft extra of blindsight until the beginning of your next turn.</li></ul><b>Sight Through Sound</b><ul><li>You have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing.</li></ul></p><hr><u>Cons</u><p><b>Blind</b><ul><li>Excluding blindsight given by Heat Vision, you are @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ADW4EH0NKRDCRCA4]{Blinded}.</li></ul><b>Blind Ignorance</b><ul><li>You can only gain heat from the Blind Thrill ability.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "stance"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": "", "style": "choice", "name": "Andabata Stance", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "none", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "fighting-stance", "dropdownOptions": ["Andabata Stance"]}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2PGSXJZ46F6EQFIM", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fighting Stance: Last Stance", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/death/skull-energy-light-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><i>Requirement:</i> When your Hit Points hit 0, if you are not killed outright then you can enter this stance as a non-action.</p><hr><p>Last stance is a special fighting stance that Gladiators can only enter under certain conditions and as a last resort.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Gladiators in last stance defy their failing bodies, staying up through force of will and the pressure alone.  They push their bodies past their limits, staying up at the cost of being fully conscious.</p><hr><u>Pros</u><p><b>Not Dead Yet</b><ul><li>When you enter this stance, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to your current heat, minimum of 1, and you remain conscious.</li></ul><b>Overdrive</b><ul><li>When you enter this stance, after gaining your temporary Hit Points, your heat is completely restored.</li></ul></p><hr><u>Cons</u><p><b>Practically Unconscious</b><ul><li>You automatically fail all Intelligence and Wisdom checks, and cannot speak intelligible words.</li></ul><b>Borrowed Time</b><ul><li>You automatically exit this stance by falling @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9KB959MRZ0H4IT4C]{Unconscious}, being healed, or being killed.  Otherwise the stance lasts 1 minute.</li></ul><b>Beyond Your Limits</b><ul><li>When you exit this stance, you take 1 point of @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion}.</li></ul><b>Bedrest</b><ul><li>You cannot enter this stance again until after a long rest.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "stance"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": "", "style": "choice", "name": "Last Stance", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "none", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "fighting-stance", "dropdownOptions": ["Last Stance"]}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "HBZQK9WH0Z4JGM8L", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fighting Stance: Scissor", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/trades/scissors-tailor-barber.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><i>Requirement:</i> Two slashing weapons.</p><hr><p>Turning your blades sideways and placing them across each other with the blades on the inside, resembling giant scissors.  You tilt your blades upward and bring them to your chest, ready to sever any part that falls between your blades by quickly yanking your blades in opposite directions.</p><hr><u>Pros</u><p><b>Disarm</b><ul><li>If a creature misses you with a melee weapon attack while you are in Self-Defense (or when not in Self-Defense at the cost of 5 heat), you can attempt to disarm the creature as a reaction (or as a non-action at the cost of 8 heat).  When you start the attempt, you make a contested attack roll using both you and the creature's current weapon.  If you succeed and the weapon can be disarmed; the creature's melee weapon is dropped in a direction of your choice within 5ft of the creature.</li></ul><b>Dis-Arm</b><ul><li>When your attack brings a humanoid's Hit Points to 0, you can spend 5 heat to instantly sever one of its limbs, giving the target a single failed Death Throw.  Doing so completely restores your heat.</li></ul></p><hr><u>Cons</u><p><b>Loose Grip</b><ul><li>Being hit by a melee weapon causes you to make a Dexterity (Save) check of DC equal to the attacking creature's Strength Attribute.  On failure, you drop one of your weapons.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "stance"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": "", "style": "choice", "name": "Scissor Stance", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "none", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "fighting-stance", "dropdownOptions": ["Scissor Stance"]}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "CO89TKPTR5S0E00L", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fighting Stance: Wrestling", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/cephalopod-octopus-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><i>Requirement:</i> Unarmed, an unarmed weapon, or improvised weapons.</p><hr><p>When death is not the intent, wrestling is a common alternative form of strength-based entertainment.  The simplest form of wrestling is to grapple and pin the another creature, a talent which wrestlers have honed through years of practice.  While variations on these rules exist, the core concept remains, and wrestling gladiators want nothing more than to score an expert pin with an audience to cheer them on.</p><hr><u>Pros</u><p><b>Wrestle Spirit</b><ul><li>Before making a Strength (Athletics) roll related to grappling, you can add +1 to your roll for every 3 heat you spend to a maximum of +5. </li></ul><b>Pinning Hold</b><ul><li>If grappling a creature of equal or smaller size, you can attempt to grapple the creature again.  If you succeed, the creature is @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.EUHT2SOTAZ1MXEDB]{Pinned} by you.  If you fail, the creature remains @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FGVFFYGPAFQGZ5RP]{Grappled}.  The pinned creature can attempt to break from this the same way as trying to break from being @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FGVFFYGPAFQGZ5RP]{Grappled}.  However, upon succeeding, the creature is no longer @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.EUHT2SOTAZ1MXEDB]{Pinned} but remains @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FGVFFYGPAFQGZ5RP]{Grappled}.</li></ul><b>Submission Hold</b><ul><li>If a creature @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.EUHT2SOTAZ1MXEDB]{Pinned} by you is unable to break out of being @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.EUHT2SOTAZ1MXEDB]{Pinned} after 3 attempts, the creature can no longer attempt to break from being @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.EUHT2SOTAZ1MXEDB]{Pinned} until it is attacked or you release it.</li><li>You gain +25 heat on the first turn that this happens.</li></ul></p><hr><u>Cons</u><p><b>Out Weight Classed</b><ul><li>You have disadvantage to grapple, or resist being @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FGVFFYGPAFQGZ5RP]{Grappled} by, creatures that are at least 1 size larger than you.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "stance"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": "", "style": "choice", "name": "Wrestling Stance", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "none", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "fighting-stance", "dropdownOptions": ["Wrestling Stance"]}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "18SU1HJZR146Z0UN", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fighting Stance: Gladiator", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You learn 2 fighting stances from the following list.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;When you can choose a new Fighting Stance as part of leveling up, you can choose from one of these Fighting Stances as well.<br><br><u><i>Fighting Stance List: Gladiator</i></u><br>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.2PGSXJZ46F6EQFIM]{Andabata Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.18SU1HJZR146Z0UN]{Wrestling Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.HBZQK9WH0Z4JGM8L]{Last Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.CO89TKPTR5S0E00L]{Scissor Stance}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "SFNDJIWCV1ORHJTM", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Dry Skin", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your fish-like body is not used to the dryness of the surface world. You must submerge in water or otherwise get soaked by 4 pints of water each day or automatically gain 1 level of @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion} at the end of your next long rest. <br />This level of exhaustion cannot be removed without submerging in water for at least 1 hour.&nbsp;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "8UMKZTEWXL5TOHF4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Extra Arms", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have two pairs of arms, with the 2nd set located beneath the first. You can choose either set of arms to complete actions with, can carry or hold things in up to all four hands, can carry up to 2 two-handed objects, and can reload up to 2 loading weapons at once without penalty.<br />However, you do not gain extra attacks, actions, or minor actions with these limbs. If you hold more than two shields, you only gain the Armor Class bonuses of the first two, as more than two becomes unwieldy and unhelpful. Additionally, while wearing any armor, shields only grant bonuses when held in 2 hands due to limited mobility.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "YLHO6P1KHCUAL9OP", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Four-Handed", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Using four hands to grip a two-handed weapon, you can double your strength modifier for damage dealt. In addition, the weapon does not count as heavy.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "60SP46N54DDHRTIR", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sunlight Sensitivity", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your time in the depths has left your eyes sensitive to the sun&rsquo;s harsh glare. You have disadvantage on attack rolls and Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight when you or what you are trying to perceive or target is in direct sunlight.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "YQWX74CA8BA3ZKDG", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Tri-Wield", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>If you are wielding at least three Light weapons without a shield, you can take a Lesser Off-Hand Attack as a non-action immediately after taking an Off-Hand Attack minor action.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "5YTUEHPZ18OHVJ18", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Amphibious", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can breathe both air and water.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "QEK74P09HWCNR1L5", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Aquatic Vocals", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your voice box is specially designed for speaking underwater. Your voice carries through water as if air, and is audible, clear, and pronounced to any creatures within 60 feet of you, distorting beyond that point.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "THVUXV1MHZ3DTIUJ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Desalination Filter", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can drink salt water as if it is fresh water.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "K9CRWETJD2UH9I7N", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Thirsty", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You must drink twice the amount of water per day to remain hydrated.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "9NXIJII89SBNXXMI", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Bite (Sa Huagin)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have a sharp set of teeth and a powerful jaw behind them. These can be used as a natural weapon that deals 1d4 piercing damage and inflicts @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.R54LQEKSDXNQ3N75]{Bleeding} on the target.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "attribute": "str", "actionType": "mwak", "chatFlavor": "Inflicts Bleeding", "damage": {"parts": [["1d4 + @mod", "piercing"]], "versatile": ""}, "proficient": true, "showInAttacks": true}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "SHZ8D3VSLPA7EC50", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Blood Frenzy", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When your Bloodsense detects a creature who has just taken damage, you can use your reaction to move adjacent to the creature and make a Bite attack against it. <br />This ability cannot move you further than 15ft.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "YVOL9DRHC1IM778U", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Bloodsense 15ft", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have incredibly well-tuned senses tuned to detect fresh blood in an instant. Within 15ft, you automatically detect and are considered to have blindsight vision on any @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.R54LQEKSDXNQ3N75]{Bleeding} creatures. Furthermore, you can detect any spilled blood fresher than a day old, and can immediately sense when a creature within range takes damage that would draw blood, such as from slashing or piercing damage. <br />While underwater, your Bloodsense range is doubled.&nbsp;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "5X6VJGSD0ZYYKWDZ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Dry Skin", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your fish-like body is not used to the dryness of the surface world. You must submerge in water or otherwise get soaked by 4 pints of water each day or automatically gain 1 level of @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion} at the end of your next long rest. <br />This level of exhaustion cannot be removed without submerging in water for at least 1 hour.&nbsp;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "NJAX0XZ39VVJ7XNE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Hemovore", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Once per long rest, if you Bite a @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.R54LQEKSDXNQ3N75]{Bleeding} creature or raw meat, you can regain hit points equal to your overall level.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Hemovore", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "ZNHVD01ULNMS0M0W", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sunlight Sensitivity", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your time in the depths has left your eyes sensitive to the sun&rsquo;s harsh glare. You have disadvantage on attack rolls and Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight when you or what you are trying to perceive or target is in direct sunlight.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "IZYTI3UCBFDKWEUU", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Dry Skin", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your fish-like body is not used to the dryness of the surface world. You must submerge in water or otherwise get soaked by 4 pints of water each day or automatically gain 1 level of @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion} at the end of your next long rest. <br />This level of exhaustion cannot be removed without submerging in water for at least 1 hour.&nbsp;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2GAA77UD05M0NG97", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Extra Arms", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have two pairs of arms, with the 2nd set located beneath the first. You can choose either set of arms to complete actions with, can carry or hold things in up to all four hands, can carry up to 2 two-handed objects, and can reload up to 2 loading weapons at once without penalty.<br />However, you do not gain extra attacks, actions, or minor actions with these limbs. If you hold more than two shields, you only gain the Armor Class bonuses of the first two, as more than two becomes unwieldy and unhelpful. Additionally, while wearing any armor, shields only grant bonuses when held in 2 hands due to limited mobility.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "XW8D056N2NFMJA8J", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Four-Handed", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Weapons with the two-handed trait do not count as heavy. In addition, it is also treated as having the Versatile trait, doubling your Strength modifier added to damage instead of increasing the die size. This versatile trait can only be activated by holding the weapon in four hands instead of two.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "81XW5LGJ382S2UUE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Improved Dual-Wield", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Holding your primary weapon in at least two hands without a shield, you can make Off-Hand attacks regardless of what weapon you use for your main attack, including a Heavy weapon.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "CWH17KUM5KF5QQSY", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sunlight Sensitivity", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your time in the depths has left your eyes sensitive to the sun&rsquo;s harsh glare. You have disadvantage on attack rolls and Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight when you or what you are trying to perceive or target is in direct sunlight.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "DRUBCSKJCK05ZOYF", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Behavioral Experience", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/diplomacy-handshake.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have advantage on Presence (Insight) checks directed at members of your adopted race.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "IRC2M1N62DQTFVBH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Cultural Osmosis", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/diplomacy-handshake.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have advantage on Intelligence (Culture) checks related to your adopted race.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "5WJE2EYK49R6V2YW", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Early Bird", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/time/day-night-sunset-sunrise.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your first ability check after a long rest has advantage.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "JQVEQW294G49HFD8", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Farmer's Advantage", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/trades/farming-planet-bulb-orange.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You add your proficiency twice to Wisdom (Nature) and Intelligence (Craft) checks in relation to farming or cooking if you are already proficient in either skill.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "1GWNHHDFP2B30LUH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Hard Sell", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/currency/coin-inset-crown-gold.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Add your proficiency twice when using Wisdom (Insight), Presence (Persuasion), or Presence (Deception) checks in relation to bartering if you are already proficient in these skills.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "AGC864XWZMAXOUFX", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Night Owl", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/raptor-owl-flying-moon.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can sleep for 1 hour less than normal during a long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "1G46RNQC5EFYGSXM", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Pet Pal", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-dog.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Add your proficiency twice to Wisdom (Instinct) checks toward domesticated beasts, such as pets and mounts, if you are already proficient in Wisdom (Instinct).", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "BX9VETXWGYCFYBBD", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Pocket Protector", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/theft-pickpocket-bribery-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You automatically have a +5 Awareness toward creatures using Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) on you.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "I7IHUKZI8GA0BZ11", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Blending In", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/chameleon-camouflage-green-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) rolls when in dense foliage, smoke, or in dim or darker light.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "PK3LAXCYY6043RY5", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Elemental Spit", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Unlike your brethren, you have to the ability to use a lesser version of the dragon&rsquo;s mighty breath weapon.&nbsp; Using an action, you can infuse your spit with elemental power and fire it at your foes.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;When you use this ability, select a single target within 30ft of you that you can see.&nbsp; Roll a ranged attack with proficiency.&nbsp; On a hit, the creature takes 2d6 damage.&nbsp; This damage increases to 3d6 at overall level 6, 4d6 at overall level 11, and 5d6 at overall level 16.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The type of damage dealt with this attack matches the element that you are resistant to with Draconic Resilience.&nbsp; You can use this ability a number of times equal to your proficiency modifier per short or long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "action", "cost": 1, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": 30, "long": 30, "units": "ft"}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "rwak", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [["2d6", "varies"]], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "proficient": true, "showInAttacks": true, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Elemental Spit", "valueFrom": "formula", "maxFormula": "@prof", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "short", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "UVQHH4CUD3D9PVZR", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fascinating Colors", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/control/buff-luck-fortune-rainbow.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have advantage on Presence (Persuasion) and Presence (Deception) checks when trying to convince someone to seem less threatening.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "ZNZV2MPB10KLX45B", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Glide", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/biological/wing-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As an action, you can choose to enter a Glide while you are airborne that lasts until you land.  While gliding: <ul><li>You may choose how far you fall at the end of each round, to a minimum of 10 feet.  You do not fall on the turn that you enter Glide.  </li><li>You can only use your movement to descend.  </li><li>For every 5 feet you fall or descend while gliding, you can move 10 feet horizontally.  </li><li>If you land while gliding, you don't take fall damage.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "8O5WZBNA6CHJTPSE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Helping Hand", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/diplomacy-handshake-gray.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can use a minor action to give an ally advantage on the next attack roll that they make.  You must end your turn adjacent to the target to do this.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2H84NPVAS7007JRB", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Lesser Flight", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/biological/wing-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have a pair of leathery dragon wings sprouting from your shoulder blades.  Your wings give you a flying speed of 30 feet.  This benefit works only in short bursts, however.  You fall if you end your turn in the air and nothing else is holding you aloft, such as Glide.  Between Limited Flight and Glide, your total horizontal movement each turn cannot exceed twice your flying speed.  You cannot fly in heavy armor.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "IX6N1K5PUGT3QCMV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sharp Claws", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/claws/claw-hooked-curved.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your claws are strong enough to do lethal damage.  They deals 1d4 slashing damage and are considered Finesse weapons.  You have proficiency for these natural weapons, and can use them to attack when you are holding nothing in them.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "attribute": "str", "actionType": "mwak", "chatFlavor": "", "damage": {"parts": [["1d4 + @mod", "slashing"]], "versatile": ""}, "proficient": true, "properties": {"amm": false, "fin": true, "foc": false, "hvy": false, "lgt": true, "lod": false, "rch": false, "spc": false, "thr": false, "two": false, "una": false, "ver": false}, "showInAttacks": true}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "1AW2E5YMMC1IGGP9", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Strength in Numbers", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain a +1 to Wisdom (Save), Intelligence (Save), and Presence (Save) checks for each ally within 10 feet, excluding yourself in any form, that isn't @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.3CQC3JEY2C3Y721F]{Incapacitated}, up to a maximum of +3.  </p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}, "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "XOU10R2EBHUGDPCQ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Tough Scales", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have natural armor equal to 12 + your Dexterity Modifier while not wearing armor.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "6H6U8OS3L3B97ICX", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Chthonic Magic", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.Q31B0A3FNPWP10MQ]{Prying Whispers} cantrip. When you reach 3rd level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.DR1S6TA7ZZHXVKVY]{Menacing Visage} spell once per long rest with this trait. When you reach 5th level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.A0XHQ6VS7PDGN9FJ]{Cloak} spell once per long rest with this trait.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "7P62CC0I70VY0V2J", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Cryptic Essence", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your chthonic attunement has deviated your very essence from the norm. As a result, certain magicks struggle to identify you as a target. <br />You have advantage on save checks against spells that can only target humanoids.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2M6GUTP8M5CJHMU5", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Darkvision 60ft", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have superior vision when peering into dark and dim light conditions. You can see in dim light within 60ft of you as if it were in bright conditions, and you can see in darkness as if it were dim conditions up to the same distance.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "DY1RSHJ35NQJIMNJ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Ominous Sight", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your darkvision is not impeded by magical darkness. <br />When you are standing in dim light or darkness, your eyes faintly glow red while conscious and not hidden by illusion. While your glowing eyes are visible, you have disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks and advantage on Presence (Intimidation) checks.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2QNO86INI4E4DGTV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Compound Eyes", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have large, rounded, compound eyes. These cannot be closed; you have no eyelids. While unconscious, you retain vision, but have half Awareness.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "TW3Q20EW6IL08P3K", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Flutter Fall", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While conscious, you can flutter your wings to prevent yourself from taking falling damage. This does not apply while wearing heavy armor.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "G7NRS6CYBK7GV2WW", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Weak Build", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your carrying capacity is reduced to 2/3 the normal amount, and you cannot grapple, trip, or shove creatures larger than you.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "9LRGBCE9H4Z9YXF9", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Elysian Magic", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.1UP8YL8Z33NMUI5P]{Minor Wonder} cantrip. When you reach 3rd level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.MRQUPL1D078DKFR2]{No Reproach} spell once per long rest with this trait. When you reach 5th level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.YCQC074MGCT6R2NY]{Ultimatum} spell once per long rest with this trait.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "LMZQYCB6DCLQ5XZL", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Healing Hands", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As an action, you can touch a creature and cause it to regain a number of hit points equal to your level. Once you use this trait, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Healing Hands", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "7N0RHPPAXR3NO2WJ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Unmistakable Presence", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Choose one Presence skill (Deception, Intimidation, Perform, or Persuasion) to be the iconic expression of your presence. If you are proficient with the chosen skill, you gain Expertise with it. If you are not proficient with the skill you become proficient, and can increase this proficiency to Expertise at any point by gaining proficiency with the skill from another source.<br />Regardless, you suffer a -1 penalty to each of the other Presence skills you did not choose for this ability.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "26VHF3075B59HT0I", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Gravitational Interference", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You subconsciously exude a field of gravity-altering magic, causing any nearby creatures to feel slightly lighter or heavier based on your attitude towards them. When creatures within 15ft of you take falling damage, you can choose to either halve it or increase the damage total by 5.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "MSF5RJ7ZU7F16G1F", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Inner Orrery", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You always know which way is up, and immediately sense when a celestial event visible from this planet is starting, such as a meteor shower, eclipse, shooting star, full or new moon, or planetary alignment.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "TYJ1AYF7FU092BN0", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sidereal Magic", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.PEHC9EYWN6B099P9]{Astral Mote} cantrip. When you reach 3rd level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.MD8DUOG1SKTK0VAC]{Stone Shot} spell once per long rest with this trait. When you reach 5th level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.XPI8O47UKUK45ZRP]{Weight of the World} spell once per long rest with this trait.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "56ALYGLX05DJKFVC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Twilight Messenger", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.OK48R80X6F22TZ7D]{Magic Missive} spell, and can cast it as a ritual. When you cast the spell, the missive folds into the shape of a moth while in flight.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "BW9HAR7W7YO0Z9PH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Enochian", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-runed-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know the language of the ancient spellcasters, and can read magic runes. You can speak, read, and write enochian, though your writings contain no power on their own.</p><p>Magic runes are now readable by you. Most runes on enchanted objects tell you what magical effect they have, sometimes also revealing the creator of the enchantment. Others leave cryptic warnings behind. You have expertise in Intelligence (Arcana) checks to interpret how a magic item works if it is adorned in magic runes.</p><p>In addition, if you fulfill a vocal component of a spell by speaking in enochian, you gain the additional charge option:</p><ul><li>2 Mana: The spell no longer requires targets to hear or understand you, and the spell&rsquo;s damage is converted to Chaos damage as it scars reality.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "QEBX3GHOS7POI4FW", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Leylines", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/runes-star-pentagon-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As a minor action, you trace a circle in the air around your feet, causing mystical and slightly glowing leylines to appear beneath you in a 5ft radius, lasting for 1 minute. Creating new leylines dissipates any previous leylines you created. Creatures within the leylines are made completely visible to all onlookers as if they could see them with true sight.</p><hr /><p><em>Requirement: </em>The <em>Slow Cast</em> ability.</p><hr /><p>While standing within your leylines, you have advantage on Concentration checks while Slow Casting, and Slow Casts can be completed with a minor action on your next turn, instead of an action.</p><hr /><p><em>Requirement: </em>The <em>Arcane Attraction</em> ability.</p><hr /><p>Leylines are also viable targets for Arcane Attraction, can be used as targets repeatedly, and can have resonance even while another resonance is active. When you first draw your leylines, they automatically resonate with you as described in the Arcane Attraction ability.</p><hr /><p><em>Requirement: </em>The <em>Up-Cast</em> ability.</p><hr /><p>While standing within your leylines, your charge limit is further increased by 1 mana.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Wizard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "XF1V319XZ78D9JGL", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Resonant Attraction", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/control/energy-stream-link-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>By bending the subspace around a creature and yourself, you can stretch the space between you and them like a rubber band. Such that, when released, the space between you ripples, flinging you toward them.</p><p>As a minor action, you can apply a magical resonance between you and another creature. The tension threatens to release, pulling you to them in an instant; resisting the pull is easy, letting go is just as easy. Only one resonance can be active at a time.</p><p>As a reaction, you can stop resisting the pull to immediately and directly move toward the resonant target up to 30 feet, stopping harmlessly adjacent to it and ending the resonance. As space bends, moving in this way feels almost like standing still, not requiring movement or affecting any simultaneous actions. However, if there is a solid obstacle between you and the target when releasing the tension, you slam into it and take falling damage for how far you moved. If @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FGVFFYGPAFQGZ5RP]{Grappled}&nbsp;or loosely bound, you take 5 chaos damage and get another (Save) check to escape. If otherwise bound, you just take the 5 chaos damage.</p><p>When you fall unconscious while this frequency is active, you are automatically pulled to the nearest resonant target.</p><p>Such a resonance can only be applied to each creature once per long rest, as the wrinkled space around a creature needs time to recover.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Wizard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "URSPXLXX4T08D0SZ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Slow Cast", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/time/hourglass-brown-orange.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Magi push their spellcasting to their limits. So long as they retain focus, their spells can shake the battlefield.</p><p>When you cast an instantaneous spell or a concentration spell that takes only 1 action to cast, you can extend the casting time to last through your next turn. When you do, you must take an action on your next turn to select the target and finish the casting or the spell fizzles. When you successfully cast a spell in this way, the spell&rsquo;s damage dice automatically roll their highest value.</p><p>You cannot take any actions or movement while casting a spell this way, or else break your concentration on the spell. If attacked during this time, you make concentration checks to try and keep the spell from failing. If you take a desperate action to cast the spell immediately, you take a point of @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion}.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Wizard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "V674JRH1IOBW11BE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Magus Spells", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-black-grey.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Wizards that specialize in becoming a Magus learn the following spells as Wizard spells once able to cast Wizard spells of the same spell level.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Magus Spells</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Able to Cast</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Spells</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1st Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-level-1.37VLMG8DVH1QVCYM]{Conduit Shock}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-level-1.93IZ61HQGJ91795Y]{Brittle Beam}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2nd Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-level-2.HVOF7QNI17K2O6C1]{Snowslide}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.XPI8O47UKUK45ZRP]{Weight of the World}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3rd Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.7UWC00HNXCOL4GFI]{Fireball}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.Z373UKDNQ9VFAMQD]{Syzygy}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4th Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>Acidic Wave*</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5th Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>---</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6th Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-6.GAC3VH4EZJOKZ8U0]{Ruin}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7th Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-7.6YF5LESOLNIOTVM1]{Despair}</p></td></tr></tbody></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "L1GHFAREZ9DVXIW0", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Up-Cast", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When casting a wizard spell, your charge limit is increased by 1 mana. For example, if 3rd level Wizard spells are the highest level you can cast, each time you cast a spell you can now spend up to 5 mana in total, instead of 4, by adding a charge option.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Wizard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "3ZNUE5OBA4KUN184", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Frost Walker", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>With military-level training, you are not slowed by non-magical rough terrain that results from ice, snow, or cold weather otherwise.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "J5VT5KLFB5OS0TQV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mystic Movement", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>If you are able to move and haven&rsquo;t yet, you can spend your movement to instead do a hypnotizing dance or flourish for another creature within 60ft that can see you. That creature gains a bonus on their next check or attack roll equal to your Proficiency Bonus.<br />Alternatively, this dance can silently convey a meaning that could be described with 5 or fewer words, regardless of language barrier. <br />This ability can be used 3 times per long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Mystic Movement", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 3, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "JFC9GWTLDKMIWYI3", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Cold Mind", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have advantage on all save checks to keep control over your emotions.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "10AP60QZ8JQR8BT7", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Incisors", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have large and powerful front teeth that can be used as natural weapons by biting into targets. These deal 1d4 piercing damage.<br />This replaces the mecian core ability &ldquo;Touch Telepathy.&rdquo;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}, "attribute": "str", "actionType": "mwak", "chatFlavor": "", "damage": {"parts": [["1d4 + @mod", "piercing"]], "versatile": ""}, "proficient": true, "showInAttacks": true}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "4SO9XWEFMEM0T29Z", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Nimble Tail", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have a thin, pink, tapered tail like that of a rat or mouse. This tail is dextrous, and able to carry and manipulate small objects and light weapons like a third hand. However, it is not dextrous enough to grant additional attacks, actions, or minor actions. <br />Shields held by this tail do not improve your Armor Class as it is not strong enough to resist any blows against the shield.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "0YU2TJMLJPZVTTPR", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Passive Reception", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>To a mecian, minds are not private&mdash;not completely. They constantly generate signals that can be &ldquo;heard&rdquo; if paid attention to. In this way, mecian minds act like an active radio receiver, constantly receiving bits of garbled information and emotion from nearby minds. This mostly comes in the form of a constant white noise, and requires some level of focus to hone in on specific neurons. When a mecian is paying attention, however, one&rsquo;s feelings can be hard to hide. <br />You have proficiency on Wisdom (Insight) skill checks made against creatures within 60ft of you. <br />Gives no benefit against Constructs or Undead.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "NG6ZJR57CL9WRGV9", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Touch Telepathy", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Mecians create a mental circuit when they touch another creature, allowing the sharing of knowledge and emotions without a single spoken word. <br />You can telepathically communicate with another creature so long as you are touching them and share a known language.<br />Cannot be used to communicate with Constructs or Undead.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "N6TTMSUFM57X8K16", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Empathic", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have an advanced capability to not just communicate and interpret thoughts, but also feelings. <br />You have advantage on Wisdom (Insight) checks against a creature whom you are touching, and are able to convey detailed emotions in a single touch. A willing creature can choose to send detailed emotions back as well. <br />Cannot use on Constructs or Undead.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "Y19AYY7DSNR7VP8F", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Imposed Impulse", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Once per long rest, as an action, you can touch a creature and force them to take a standard action. Cannot use on Constructs or Undead.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Imposed Impulse", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "TMFEJKD6VESCN6XL", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Tri-Wield", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>If you are wielding at least three Light weapons without a shield, you can take a Off-Hand Attack and Lesser Off-Hand Attack on the same turn, using a different weapon for each attack.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "WRPRF15WQAE8RENU", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Bull Rush", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While <em>Dashing</em>, you can make one attack using your Horns as a minor action before the end of your turn.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "FSYAETXYEA3YJSPS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Horns", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have a pair of large horns growing from your head. These function as a natural weapon that deals 1d8 piercing damage.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}, "attribute": "str", "actionType": "mwak", "chatFlavor": "", "damage": {"parts": [["1d8 + @mod", "piercing"]], "versatile": ""}, "proficient": true, "showInAttacks": true}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "8PHJHUPTCSNNWE71", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Trailblazer", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You always know which way is north, and you can accurately retrace your steps along any path you have traveled within the past 7 days.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "K44RS5GZ07MOGUI1", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Frost Walker", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have hooves that are broad, flat but coarse, and deeply cloven compared to other minotaur. This allows you to walk atop soft snow and retain a grip on slickened ice. <br />Your hooves prevent you from being slowed by non-magical rough terrain that results from ice, snow, or cold weather otherwise.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "PO72QLL7HDNVWOUP", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Tundra Heart", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Every part of your body is built for self-regulation, from hide to horn to hoof. So much so, that your fur is said to be somewhat magic resistant, and horns magic conductive. Regardless of magical inclination, this causes more physical magics to shirk off of frost-hides. <br />You have advantage on all Constitution (Save) Checks against magic.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "FTOHE443QKI6XBGG", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Architectural Intuition", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain one of the following traits:<ul><li>With proficiency in the Building Trade, when you are hitting a structure with a weapon attack, you can angle the impact in a way that is most likely to weaken its structural integrity. On a successful DC 12 Intelligence (Investigation) check, you permanently create a structural weakness and can immediately apply the Building Trade&rsquo;s <strong>Destruct </strong>bonus to this attack.</li><li>With proficiency in the Pathfinding Trade, when you take the <em>Explore Area</em> rest action in a city, ruins, or other constructed environment, you have advantage on the associated skill check.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "7IE9OGRPT50ZUUAY", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Bull in a Potion Shop", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you hit a creature your size or smaller with a natural weapon attack, you can push it 5ft away from you. If this movement is obstructed, increase the attack&rsquo;s damage die size by two steps.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "A3ZYWKJ6CPWV2VAL", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spatial Reconstruction", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Once they&rsquo;ve surveyed a location, mason-minds never forget it, and can navigate it again with great ease, even in the dark. With just a glance, mason-minds can make reliable inferences about a structure they haven&rsquo;t fully explored based on the parts they have. For example, should one door or passageway become impassable, they&rsquo;re able to quickly reroute. <br />You can close your eyes and picture an environment&rsquo;s basic layout inside and out as you last knew it. Details however, such as colors, textures, small objects, creatures, etc. are not retained any better than an average creature&rsquo;s memory.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "76S5EYBF31K9S9L4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Heavy Hitter", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you make a Strength-based attack with a weapon or improvised weapon, the weapon&rsquo;s damage die is increased by one step.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "27PZP21ZBZM74HM9", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Runners High", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Once per rest, when you <em>Dash</em> you can spend a rest die to gain temporary hit points equal to a roll of the die plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1).</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Runners High", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "short", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "0FT24V5W1898J73O", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Stamina Reserve", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you spend a rest die, you can increase its size by one step (to a maximum of 1d12) before rolling it. You can use this ability a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and can spend multiple uses on the same rest die. You regain all expended uses on a long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Stamina Reserve", "valueFrom": "formula", "maxFormula": "@prof", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "EKFZ9KVQTVVV81BU", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Lesser Horns", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have a pair of horns growing from your head. These function as a natural weapon that deals 1d4 piercing damage.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}, "attribute": "str", "actionType": "mwak", "chatFlavor": "", "damage": {"parts": [["1d4 + @mod", "piercing"]], "versatile": ""}, "proficient": true, "showInAttacks": true}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "HF5TGW1UQJY6J1GK", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spirit Guidance", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>In moments of hesitation, you can draw upon the bond you have with your familiar, leaning on their instincts to pull you through. Before making a Wisdom check, you can choose to add your proficiency bonus to the roll&rsquo;s total, so long as you can see your conjoined familiar. You can use this ability once per rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Guidance", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "short", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "1THSTBQHCP5YUGKL", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spirit Guide", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You learn the spell @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.TT94JMKOUYP2WM96]{Cojoin Familiar} and can cast it once per long rest without expending material components.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "RZSLDAG5NL15FBEM", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Armiger's Armory", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-weapons-orange.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain proficiency in one weapon of your choice and one of the following:</p><ul><li>One additional weapon of your choice</li><li>Light armor</li><li>Medium armor</li><li>Shields</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "29L79CWTS5SNA9ES", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Impossible Stance", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/maneuver-greatsword-yellow.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<hr/><p><em>Requirement: </em>The <em>Fighting Stance</em> ability from the <em>Fighter</em> class.</p><hr/><p><em>Using magic to sharpen your focus and give stability to your stances, you&rsquo;re able to make up for weaknesses that proficiency alone cannot solve. </em></p><p>When entering a Fighting Stance, you can choose to spend Mana equal to your proficiency bonus to ignore 1 of the Stance&rsquo;s Cons.</p><p>When switching between Fighting Stances, you can spend the same Mana to retain one of the previous Stance&rsquo;s Pros.</p><p>In addition, learn 1 Fighting Stance when you gain this ability.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Wizard Starter Abilities and the Fighting Stance ability from the Fighter class.", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "AJ29PDCH81I8B27R", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spell Armor", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/defensive/shield-barrier-flaming-diamond-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>You&rsquo;ve learned to always keep an imperceptible aura of magic around you, reinforcing your thoughts and body and merging with the energies of your mystic arts. </em></p><p>While conscious, you can add your Intelligence modifier to Concentration checks. <br />In addition, you gain each of the following bonus abilities, so long as you meet their requirements:</p><br><hr/><p><em>Requirement: </em>The <em>Spellarm</em> ability.</p><hr/><p>While <em>Spellarm</em> is active, you are resistant to up to two of the spell&rsquo;s damage types.</p><br><hr/><p><em>Requirement: </em>The <em>Sword and Sorcery</em> ability.</p><hr/><p>When you cast a cantrip with a casting time of 1 action, you can take the <strong>Self-Defense</strong> action as a minor action.</p><br><hr/><p><em>Requirement: </em>The <em>Impossible Stance </em>ability.</p><hr/><p>When you would be forced out of a Fighting Stance, such as from being knocked <strong>Prone</strong> or losing a Stance&rsquo;s requirements, you can make a Concentration check to attempt to remain in your Fighting Stance regardless. On a success, you can remain in your stance so long as you correct the problem before the end of your next turn.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Wizard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "M8U825D68XPJKC0Q", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spellarm", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-axe-energy-pink.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Magic is powerful, mysterious, but often the hardest part about it is that it lacks form. Spells, especially powerful ones, often require some form of stability or backbone to act as a conduit, especially over time. The school of enchantment knows this all too well. </em></p><p><em>It&rsquo;s the same when it comes to combat. While most mystics will point a wand or staff to bring their magic to bear against a foe, an armiger has found great success in sustaining a magic&rsquo;s potency by wreathing their armaments in spellcraft. </em></p><p>You gain an additional charge option that can be applied to spells with an instantaneous duration:</p><ul><li>x2 Total Mana Cost: You imbue this spell or cantrip into a weapon you are holding for the next 1 minute with Concentration. The imbuement is lost should you lose Concentration on it, or another creature takes possession of the weapon. <br />The first time this imbued weapon or its ammunition strikes a target each round, the following happens:</li><ul><li>The weapon&rsquo;s damage die is two sizes smaller.</li><li>The stored spell is cast on the target originating from the weapon, even if the spell&rsquo;s target is &ldquo;Self.&rdquo;</li><li>The spell&rsquo;s first spell attack automatically hits.</li></ul></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Wizard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "Y5PXHIVN1CM6H74J", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mystic Armiger Spells", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/books/symbol-axe-gold-grey.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Wizards that specialize in becoming a Mystic Armiger learn the following spells as Wizard spells once able to cast Wizard spells of the same spell level.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Mystic Armiger Spells</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Able to Cast</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Spells</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Wizard Cantrips</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.P8AYYAYOXXDCGM9B]{Brace for Impact}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.MB7NWQ5H11LSIVV7]{Caustic Needle}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.0JWJ9J7A2AMSNDK0]{Jolt}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1st Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.LO6PLV28RA6CBCLU]{Burst Into Flames}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2nd Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.3BUFFKXCN0WVRIMP]{Barrier}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.MFJSEGIJAH0UIH47]{Identify}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3rd Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.6GFN59MWTZPMBQ61]{Haste}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4th Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-4.7H0M1UB9Z1ZVHSJ0]{Remove Arms}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6th Level Wizard Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-6.3I736YDSAFN1B3E3]{Hundred Spear Assault}</p></td></tr></tbody></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "QI8Z7PCV0BBCVFXO", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sword and Sorcery", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/blade-tip-energy-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>When skilled enough in both arts, swinging a sword is no different from slinging a cantrip. Both require an instinct and willingness to kill. </em></p><p>When you cast a cantrip with a casting time of 1 action, you can make a single weapon attack as a minor action. This attack does not add your attribute modifier to its damage.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Wizard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "VG98NJ22142VHWO6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Multiplicity", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/defensive/illusion-evasion-echo-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Unlock: </em>When you reach 6th level overall you may take the ability below</p><p>One of the Ninja&rsquo;s greatest abilities is to create copies of themselves and employ them in combat or use them to aid in deceit.&nbsp; As an Action a Ninja may create a Copy of themselves in a space adjacent to them.&nbsp; It costs 1 Spirit per Copy made, and a ninja can make 1 Copy at 6th level and 2 Copies at 12th level.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Copies move when you do in the initiative order and their actions are controlled by you.&nbsp; On the first turn summoned, a Copy may only move or take an action.&nbsp; After the turn they were summoned, a Copy may make an action and a move action.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A Copy has the following statistics:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Base stats, skills, and proficiencies are identical to yours</li><li>A Copy has no class features aside from Sneak Attack and any Ninja abilities you possess at time of creation, aside from Multiplicity.</li><ul><li>A Copy&rsquo;s Sneak Attack deals 2d6 damage.&nbsp; When you hit 12th level, it goes up to 3d6.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><li>Hit Points equal to your overall character level + your proficiency bonus</li><li>They must spend Spirit to use Ninja abilities as the base class states</li><li>Spirit equal to half your proficiency bonus</li><li>They are wearing the same armor as you, and carry a copy of a single weapon on your person, but gain none of your other equipment.&nbsp; Any magical effects from your weapon or armor does not work for your Copy</li><li>A Copy gains the following abilities as well:&nbsp;</li><ul><li>Shared Mind: A Copy knows everything that its creator knows, including languages.&nbsp; As well, everything that a Copy senses is known to its creator, provided they are on the same plane, and even over great distances.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Telepathic Bond: While a Copy is on the same plane as its creator, it can share what it senses with them and communicate telepathically.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><li>A Copy lasts for 1 minute after summoned before vanishing</li><li>Should their Hit Points drop to 0, or their Spirit drop to 0, a Copy and all equipment they were created with, vanishes</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "6th level overall, must have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "ILG1OGOCEP2L619C", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mystic Seals", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/runes-star-magenta.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Ninjas can evoke special mystic abilities through the use of Spirit and a combination of hand seals.&nbsp; You learn these Mystic Seals over time, receiving Detonate upon taking this ability, and the others you gain the other Ninja abilities as specified in their descriptions:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Detonate</strong></p><p>As a Minor Action you can spend 1 Spirit to imbue a piece of ammunition or a thrown weapon with the ability to explode on a successful strike, causing them to deal an extra 1d6 force damage to the target.&nbsp; This enhancement lasts until used or the end of your next turn.&nbsp; Whichever comes first.&nbsp; The thrown weapon or ammunition used is destroyed in the process.</p><p>Alternatively, you can instead spend 1 Spirit as part of your Attack Action and make a finesse unarmed attack against a target.&nbsp; On a success, the target takes 2d6 force damage from a small explosion originating at the point which you struck them, in addition to normal unarmed damage.&nbsp; Should you have the ability to make more than one attack a turn, this ability only takes up one.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Sudden Fog</strong></p><p><em>Unlock:</em> Received upon taking Run Like The Wind.</p><p>As an Action you can spend 1 Spirit to create a fog in your current space that has a 10 foot radius.&nbsp; The fog heavily obscures the area it covers and allows you to immediately make a Dexterity (Stealth) check after it is created.&nbsp; The fog lasts for 1 minute before dissipating.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Hide Below</strong></p><p><em>Unlock:</em> Received upon taking Shadow Walk.</p><p>This ability can be cast in two different ways:&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As an Action: you can spend 1 Spirit to sink into the ground beneath you, provided its solid stone, dirt, or sand.&nbsp; The space you are sinking into must be large enough to fully contain your body.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>You are hidden beneath the ground giving you complete concealment.&nbsp; While hidden you have 0 speed, have disadvantage on Dexterity (Save) checks, and can take no action other than resurfacing as a minor action.&nbsp; You can still hear and discern through listening what is going on above you and can tell when a creature is within 10 feet of you.</p><p>After 1 minute of hiding in this way, you have the choice of spending 1 Spirit to stay hidden, or resurface as a minor action and take the rest of your turn.&nbsp; Should you have 0 Spirit at the start of your turn while this ability is active, you immediately resurface.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Should the space where you are hiding be destroyed, you surface immediately and are ejected 5 feet in a random direction.&nbsp; If not possible, you simply surface immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Taking 10 Minutes: to use this ability causes it to act as it is described above with a couple exceptions:</p><ul><li>You only have to spend 1 Spirit for the initial cast and for every 10 minutes you are hidden this way</li><li>You can hear up to 15 feet around you</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Substitution</strong></p><p><em>Unlock:</em> Received upon taking Multiplicity.</p><p>As a reaction when you take damage, you can spend 1 Spirit to switch places with a Copy that you have created with Multiplicity.&nbsp; The Copy must be within 60 feet to do so, and it takes the damage instead of you.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "PLHRF3R67K6ELYGN", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Run Like The Wind", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-glowing-yellow.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>A Ninja must be ready to move through any terrain and cross any obstacle to accomplish their goals.&nbsp; With this ability you can walk across water as if it were solid ground, as long as you do not start or end your turn on or in the water.&nbsp; Should you end your turn over water, you may spend 1 Spirit to stay standing on its surface and continue walking across the water next turn.&nbsp; If you started in water, you may spend 1 Spirit to rise to its surface and walk across it.<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Additionally, you may spend 1 Spirit on your turn to gain one of the following abilities until the start of your next turn.&nbsp; You may have more than one of these active at a time, but each one still costs 1 Spirit:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Walk across other liquids as if they were water, using the same rules stated above.</li><li>Walk along walls as though they were flat terrain.</li><li>Ignore rough terrain.</li><li>Run across a gap, chasm, etc.&nbsp; as long as you start and end your movement on solid ground.&nbsp; This kind of movement can only be made horizontally.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "1N6CJP6HAF725FR3", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Shadow Walk", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/mammals/wolf-shadow-black.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Shadows are your home and the terrain in which you excel the most.  While in shadows or moving while Stealthed your movement speed is doubled.  Additionally, while using the Hide action, Stealthed, or in shadows, others have disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to notice you.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "GQTOQHRNTQNSYXX6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spirit", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/nature/tree-spirit-glow-black-yellow.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Spirit energy is the inner power that a Ninja harnesses to perform great feats of supernatural power and evoke the elements in specific ways.&nbsp; A number of the Ninja&rsquo;s abilities rely on spending Spirit to make them happen.&nbsp; The amount of Spirit you have is equal to:&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>4 + your proficiency bonus + either your Intelligence or Presence modifier (whichever is higher)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You regain all of your Spirit after a long rest, and a short rest restores an amount of Spirit equal to your proficiency bonus.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Spirit", "valueFrom": "formula", "maxFormula": "4+@prof+max(@int,@pre)", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "short", "rechargeStyle": "gain", "rechargeFormula": "@prof", "rechargeMessage": "Regain all on a Long Rest", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "JQ3I9PYSEKDJ5F06", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Way of the Ninja", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/weapons/swords/sword-katana.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain proficiency in Intelligence (Arcana) and either dagger, midsword, or throwing star.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "6HKS62RNGHEOJFHU", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Concurrency", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/time/hourglass-tilted-glowing-gold.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When an ally takes their turn directly before you, or else you take your turn directly before an ally, you can spend a Reaction to instead share a turn.  On a shared turn, each creature's Actions, Minor Actions, Reactions, or Desperate Actions can be taken in any order between creatures who share a turn.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For each Growth Level, another ally with an adjacent turn can join the shared turn.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Order Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "YOHN2SD20CALZT81", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Act: Divine Average", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/trading-justice-scale-gold.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><p>You can spend @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Dice in the following ways:</p><ul><li><strong>Divine Average:</strong> Spend a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die before you roll a skill check or attack roll to automatically roll 10 instead. This does not count as an Eikonic Number.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Order Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "QRO01LDH2F2Y4XKO", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Divine Commandment", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/control/control-influence-crown-gold.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As a Minor Action, you can proclaim 1 <strong>Divine Commandment</strong> from the <em>Divine Commandment Table</em> below.&nbsp; For the next 1 minute, you radiate a 60ft radius sphere of divine aura that binds all creatures within by said <strong>Divine Commandment</strong>, so long as they have an intelligence of 6 or higher.&nbsp; Creatures are only bound by the commandment while in the radius, and they innately know when they are under the effects of the commandment, even if they did not hear the pronouncement.&nbsp; All creatures within the radius understand the conditions of the commandment, even if they share no languages with you.&nbsp; During the duration, you can use a Minor Action to proclaim a new Divine Commandment, but the duration does not reset.&nbsp; You can use this ability once per Rest and you gain an additional usage of this ability at each Growth Level.</p><p>During the duration, if you see a creature break the commandment, then as a Reaction you can announce the offender and either make one weapon attack or a melee spell attack that deals 1d10 + your Wisdom Modifier Radiant Damage on hit.  If the target would be out of range, a holy weapon duplicating your own briefly conjures adjacent to the target to attack instead.  Either way, this attack has advantage and ignores cover.</p><p>If you break your own Divine Commandment, you lose 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.&nbsp; If you have no @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Dice, the Divine Commandment ends and you cannot make the same Divine Commandment until your next Rest.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Divine Commandments Table</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Commandments</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Law Breaking</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&ldquo;Be silent.&rdquo;</p></td><td><p>Talking; using spells with a Vocal component or listed audio effect.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&ldquo;Cease flight.&rdquo;</p></td><td><p>Starting flying or ending your turn while flying.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&ldquo;Conserve energy.&rdquo;</p></td><td><p>Charging a spell.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&ldquo;Do not bear false witness.&rdquo;</p></td><td><p>Saying something this Cleric sincerely and totally believes to be false.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&ldquo;No loitering.&rdquo;</p></td><td><p>Not using movement speed before the end of your turn.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&ldquo;No running.&rdquo;</p></td><td><p>Dash Action.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&ldquo;No violence.&rdquo;</p></td><td><p>Dealing damage.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&ldquo;Remain orderly.&rdquo;</p></td><td><p>Take a Desperate Action.&nbsp;</p></td></tr></tbody></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Order Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Commandment", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "short", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "4298EW53PUXRT405", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Number of Order", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/cog-orange-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain a new Eikonic Number which serves as your <strong>Eikonic Number of Order</strong> (see the &ldquo;Eikonic Numbers&rdquo; Cleric Starter Ability for details).</p><p>You also gain access to the following <strong>Mantras</strong>, which can only be assigned to your <strong>Eikonic Number of Order</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Justice Never Rests:</strong> You gain an extra Reaction until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Lawful:</strong> You immediately know either:</li><ul><li>An important law, natural or legal, of the area you are in.</li><li>Someone who has broken the law in the last 24 hours within 1 mile of you.</li></ul><li><strong>Oath to Order</strong>: Move an event or creature&rsquo;s turn up or back in the Initiative Order by 1 slot. This can only affect the same target once per turn.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": "?", "style": "single", "name": "Eikon: Order", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": "?", "rechargeOn": "none", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "NU56ZP100JW4HO08", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Law Abiding", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/cog-orange-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Once per long rest, when you enter into an agreement that would reasonably be beneficial for at least the other creature, you are bound by your word.  You gain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die upon completing the agreement without breaking the terms.  You lose a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die if you break the terms of the agreement.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Law Abiding", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "HAM7R26DCCISOZJH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Refined Magicks", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/cog-orange-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain proficiency in Intelligence (Arcana) if you were not already proficient in it.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "NON1FUV6X5DENLGZ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Order Dominion Spells", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/cog-orange-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Clerics of the Order Dominion learn the following spells when able to cast Cleric spells of the same spell level.&nbsp; These spells are always prepared and don&rsquo;t count against your prepared spell amount.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Dominion spells are considered Cleric spells when learned this way.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Order Dominion Spells</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Able to Cast</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Spells</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1st Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.MRQUPL1D078DKFR2]{No Reproach}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.3XZ089KFBQMQUFK5]{Tunnel Vision}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2nd Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.RSOH8YFIDRSE3ZCL]{Repress Emotions}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.YCQC074MGCT6R2NY]{Ultimatum}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3rd Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.XD6W9NSEKZ48HGCD]{Dispel Magic}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.Z373UKDNQ9VFAMQD]{Syzygy}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4th Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-4.XJ75LFYCND9DK4GP]{Banish}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-4.7H0M1UB9Z1ZVHSJ0]{Remove Arms}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5th Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-5.N2ZSVB7D1W068EWZ]{Ashame}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-5.J9QLMOBH6NXLN5OQ]{Telepathic Network}</p></td></tr></tbody></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "3K61WI41NGFFQZL2", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Cheap Shot", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-dagger-white-orange.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>In the heat of combat there are no rules keepers, just victors and corpses. </em></p><p>After rolling for damage on an attack, you can use the following table to reduce the final damage in order to either make the target save against a <strong>condition</strong>, or automatically apply a <strong>condition</strong> to your target. Unless listed as indefinite, Cheap Shot conditions apply until the end of your next turn.</p><p><em>Cheap Shot Table</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Damage Cost (Save)</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Damage Cost (Automatic)</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Applied Condition</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>The target gains a stack of indefinite @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.R54LQEKSDXNQ3N75]{Bleeding}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>The target becomes @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.WK17M9FZR08DRUP1]{Deafened}.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>The target gains 2 stacks of indefinite @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.R54LQEKSDXNQ3N75]{Bleeding}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>The target becomes @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.LM1J0T2XZ0KS1UFK]{Muddled}.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>The target gains 3 stacks of indefinite @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.R54LQEKSDXNQ3N75]{Bleeding}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>12</p></td><td><p>The target becomes @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FIKTMW8NEOFEAKG6]{Hobbled}.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>14</p></td><td><p>The target becomes @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.3BAHKVP3ZKFC7BJD]{Staggered}.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>The target becomes @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9X088PM7H5U2S1HQ]{Sickened}.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>15</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>The target becomes @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ADW4EH0NKRDCRCA4]{Blinded}.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>The DC for this ability is:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>8 + your proficiency modifier + half of the number of your Sneak Attack dice (minimum 1)</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Rogue", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "single", "name": "Cheap Shot DC", "valueFrom": "formula", "maxFormula": "8+@prof+ceil(@vital/2)", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "none", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "XIJRUICHXRXLH3K6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Evasive", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/fire/explosion-embers-evade-silhouette.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Your finely honed agility and alertness has given you the uncanny ability to scrape through otherwise deadly situations.&nbsp;</em></p><p><strong>Quick Escape</strong></p><p>If an attacker that you can see hits you with an attack, you can use your reaction to add +2 to your AC. If this causes the attack to miss, you take no damage and can immediately <strong>Disengage</strong> and move up to half your speed.</p><p><strong>Evasive Maneuver</strong></p><p>When making a Dexterity (Save) check to take half damage from an effect, you instead take no damage when you would take half damage, and half damage when you would take full damage.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "adept"}, "requirements": "6th level overall and 3rd level Rogue", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "X90JYLUREXENZDQC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Expertise", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/trades/academics-merchant-scribe.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Despite acting outside of traditional means, rogues are often highly trained experts in their fields. Any less and they could be replaced or worse.</em></p><p>Choose two skills that you are proficient in. Gain <strong>expertise </strong>in those skills.</p><p>See &ldquo;<em>Chapter 6 - How To Play</em>&rdquo; for more info on Expertise.</p><p>Pick another proficient skill to gain Expertise in when you reach 5th level overall, 11th level overall while at Adept Rogue, and at 17th level overall while at Expert Rogue.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "novice"}, "requirements": "Must have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "5H1YLH3E742DLXDK", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Exploit", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-dagger-blood-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>When an opponent leaves an opening, there is no choice but to take advantage of it. </em></p><p>When landing a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.1P8DJ5ZSPPJRMLWH]{Vital Strike} on a creature with one of the following conditions, you can Exploit the condition to:</p><ul><li>Remove the condition.</li><li>Increase the attack&rsquo;s damage by +1 per condition tier.</li><li>Using the table below, apply a lesser condition to the target.</li></ul><p>For conditions resulting from other conditions, such as @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.3CQC3JEY2C3Y721F]{Incapacitated} being applied as the result of a target being @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.OBTES08D2XC130IG]{Paralyzed}, you can only exploit the overarching condition. After exploiting a creature, it becomes immune to Exploit until the end of its next turn. Unless listed as indefinite, Exploit conditions apply until the end of your next turn.</p><p><em>Exploit Table</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Condition Tier</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Exploitable Conditions</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Exploit Effect</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Low Tier</p></td><td><p>1 Bleeding, Deafened, Hobbled, Muddled, Staggered</p></td><td><p>None.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Mid Tier</p></td><td><p>3 Bleeding, Charmed, Frenzied, Frightened, Grappled, Prone, *Villainized</p></td><td><p>Apply one of the following conditions to the target:&nbsp;</p><p>1 @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.R54LQEKSDXNQ3N75]{Bleeding} (indefinite), @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.WK17M9FZR08DRUP1]{Deafened}, @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FIKTMW8NEOFEAKG6]{Hobbled}, @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.LM1J0T2XZ0KS1UFK]{Muddled}, or @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.3BAHKVP3ZKFC7BJD]{Staggered}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>High Tier</p></td><td><p>Blinded, Pinned, Restrained, Sickened, Silenced</p></td><td><p>Apply one of the following conditions to the target:&nbsp;</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.conditions.UK95BQ45TGSD5Q3V]{Frightened}, @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FGVFFYGPAFQGZ5RP]{Grappled}, or @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.RK3DF56CKMQUV6DM]{Prone}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Max Tier</p></td><td><p>Incapacitated, Unconscious, Stunned, Paralyzed</p><br /><br /></td><td><p>Apply one of the following conditions to the target:&nbsp;</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ADW4EH0NKRDCRCA4]{Blinded}, @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9X088PM7H5U2S1HQ]{Sickened}, @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.GVNYWJ2OSBQN7YC3]{Silenced}</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>*Villainized: Applied by Bards.</p><p>At 5th level overall, 11th level overall while at Adept Rogue, and at 17th level overall while at Expert rogue, increase the damage added by 1 die size.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "novice"}, "requirements": "Must have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "JXY8GNKY37UR93L6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Lightning Reflex", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/movement/arrow-upward-yellow.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>In moments of import, you&rsquo;ve learned to let your reflexes take control. Nothing&rsquo;s faster or more reliable in a pinch. </em></p><p><br />During a Desperate Action, you can do one of the following as a non-action: <strong>Dash</strong>, <strong>Disengage</strong>, <strong>Hide</strong>, or <strong>Search</strong>.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Must have a Rogue Adept Ability", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "MK99LKGD8IHJ48QD", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Slippery", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Where others see obstacles, rogues see opportunities.</em></p><p>The <strong>Dash</strong>, <strong>Disengage</strong>, <strong>Hide</strong>, and <strong>Search</strong> actions are now minor actions.</p><p>Once per turn, you can take either the <strong>Give, Take, or Trade</strong> minor action or the <strong>Hide</strong> minor action as a non-action.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "adept"}, "requirements": "6th level overall and 3rd level Rogue", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "T4YIHUPQPW9YAAV6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Speak in Code", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-symbol-triangle-pink.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Either during your formal training, from a run in with another Rogue, or some other happenstance of the profession, you have in some way, shape, or form, come to understand the Code of Thieves'.  It is a specific way of speaking that hides messages in plain speech through shifts in utterance, jargon, and turns of phrases.  Additionally, there is also a short hand and special symbolic signage that is used to help relay simplistic information, such as locations, territory, sanctuary, and marks for instance.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Only others that know the Code of Thieves' can understand it, and speaking it takes four times longer to get an idea across than it would simply saying it in layman's terms.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Rogue", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "A3GDM85RSHS80N3U", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Vital Strike", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-dagger-white-orange.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Through experience and cunning you know exactly where a strike would be most fatal and how to do it with subtlety. </em></p><p>Once per turn, you can deal extra damage to a target equal to one of your weapon damage types. When attacking with a Light or Finesse weapon, or else a natural weapon, Vital Strike will activate if any of the following is true:</p><ul><li>You have <strong>advantage</strong> on the attack.&nbsp;</li><li>You are <strong>unseen</strong> by the target.</li><li>The target has one or more <strong>conditions</strong>.</li></ul><p>The amount of damage that a Vital Strike deals increases as you gain levels in the Rogue class, as shown in the table below:</p><p><em>Vital Strike Table</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Vital Strike Level*</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Extra Damage</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1-2</p></td><td><p>1d6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3-4</p></td><td><p>2d6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5-6</p></td><td><p>3d6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7-8</p></td><td><p>4d6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>9-10</p></td><td><p>5d6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>11-12</p></td><td><p>6d6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>13-14</p></td><td><p>7d6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>15-16</p></td><td><p>8d6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>17</p></td><td><p>9d6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>18</p></td><td><p>10d6</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>*Vital Strike Level is equal to your Rogue level, plus &frac12; of every non-Rogue level, rounded down. For example, a level 7 Wizard / Level 4 Rogue would have a Vital Strike Level of 7, and could thus deal 4d6 Vital Strike damage.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Rogue", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "actionType": "abil", "damage": {"parts": [["@vitald6", "weapon damage"]], "versatile": ""}, "showInAttacks": true}, "folder": null, "_id": "1P8DJ5ZSPPJRMLWH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sunlight Sensitivity", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/perception/eye-tendrils-web-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While in sunlight, you have disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "0YK75ZQYDRVHEP50", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Five-Finger Discount", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/bones/bones-hand-grey.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>A thief&rsquo;s hands are trained in delicate procedures, a natural quickness that allows for sneaky operations. As thieves act throughout the day, their mental and physical acuity is drained, until they inevitably botch an attempt. Thieves sometimes call these &ldquo;Thief Fingers&rdquo; or simply Fingers (with a capital F), referring to how many more tricks the thief can pull off before failing.</p><p>You have 5 &ldquo;Fingers&rdquo; (regardless of how many <em>fingers</em> you have) which represent the deftness of your most thieving faculties. They can be spent to take certain Thief actions.</p><p>Fingers are regained at the end of a rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 5, "style": "counter", "name": "Fingers", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 5, "rechargeOn": "short", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "folder": null, "_id": "EE5KJBK43K69MTT5", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Kleptomania", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/equipment/hand/glove-simple-leather-brown-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you thieve, you feel a rush of adrenaline&mdash;a high off of the excitement of repossession, regardless of the worth of the item itself. This feeling keeps you moving, and keeps you on your toes as you make your escape.</p><p>After successfully stealing something, you can:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Disengage as a non-action.</li><li>Until the start of your next turn, move through the space of other creatures at half speed, should you have been blocked by them instead.</li><li>For the next minute, gain temporary hit points equal to your proficiency bonus at the start of your turn.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "POBHBOBIFM6899DA", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Master Thief", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/currency/coin-embossed-ruby-gold.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Thieves are skilled in the art of the transition. The transition of one&rsquo;s attention from here to there. The transition of items of theirs to yours. The transition of here and gone.</p><p>As a master thief, you gain the following Thief abilities:</p><p><strong>Steal (1 Finger)</strong></p><p>As an action, you swipe a random item from a creature within 5 feet of you. Roll a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check, with advantage if they don&rsquo;t know that you&rsquo;re there, and with disadvantage if they are actively hostile toward or suspicious of you.</p><p>Regardless of the result, you steal one item from the target as determined by the GM, with higher results meaning you swipe larger or rarer items from the target&rsquo;s possession. With this ability, you cannot steal any items they are being directly held or clutched, or that are not easily detachable, nor items they do not possess.</p><p>If the creature has no separate items or equipment in their possession, or if it would better match the Steal roll&rsquo;s result, you instead break, tear, or cut off a piece of the creature to take as an item. As a result, the creature&rsquo;s natural weapons are reduced by 1 die size. This can only be done once per creature, and lasts until their next long rest.</p><p><strong>Swipe (3 Fingers)</strong></p><p>As an action, you attempt to take a held or clutched weapon or item from a creature within 5 feet of you. Roll a contested Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check against the target. If you succeed, you take the item from their hand, and are proficient in the weapon for the next 1 minute.</p><p>If the stolen item is a weapon, you can immediately make an attack against the target using this weapon.</p><p><strong>Mug</strong></p><p>If you hit a creature as part of the Attack Action, you can use either Steal or Swipe against that creature as a Minor Action before the end of your turn.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "NFT3RSXOWDP7SS1X", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spell Thief", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/unholy/hand-marked-pink.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While most thieves steal or borrow possessions, some thieves specialize in the thievery of the arcane. It turns out, many of the principles are the same: lower a target&rsquo;s defenses, move in, and take what you want. However, instead of a pocket, you&rsquo;re reaching into their soul or otherwise.</p><p>While harder to fence, spell thieves are particularly adept in combat scenarios and at taking on spellcasters&mdash;many of them are spellcasters themselves. Indeed, the art of spell thievery is sometimes cultivated in military and mercenary bands for its anti-magical talents.</p><p>As a spell thief, you gain the following Thief abilities:</p><p><strong>Strip Down (2 Fingers)</strong></p><p>As a minor action, steal a non-instantaneous magical or spell effect off of another creature that is within 5ft of you and place it on yourself. If the spell effect required concentration, you now maintain that concentration for the remainder of its duration. An effect that lasts longer than 24 hours cannot be stolen.</p><p><strong>Lost Marbles (2 Fingers)</strong></p><p>Replacing 3d6 Sneak Attack, you can steal 1 Mana from a creature, turning into a small marble-sized mote of solid Mana.</p><p>Mana Motes can be absorbed as a Minor Action to gain 1 Mana. If not used within 1 hour, the Mana Mote dissipates.</p><p><strong>Spell Steal (2 Fingers)&nbsp;</strong></p><p>As a reaction to a cantrip being cast within 30 ft of you, you can spend 2 Fingers to attempt to steal their knowledge of the cantrip. The caster must succeed on a Concentration check versus your Sneak Attack DC or else the spell fails, you temporarily learn the cantrip, and they are unable to cast the cantrip again until their next long rest. On a success, you fail to steal the cantrip and they cast the spell normally.</p><p>When you learn a cantrip from this ability, choose Intelligence, Wisdom, or Presence to be your spellcasting attribute for the cantrip. If the cantrip has verbal components, you must be able to hear the caster to learn it, likewise if it has somatic or material components you must be able to see the caster to learn it.</p><p>You forget the cantrip learned from this ability when you finish a rest or learn a different cantrip using this ability. However, each time you finish a rest, you can choose not to forget your current cantrip at the cost of not regaining one of your expended Fingers.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "26JCNSTKXQ52FM2O", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sticky Fingers", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/webs/web-spider-caught-hand-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain proficiency in two of the following:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Dexterity (Sleight of Hand)</li><li>Dexterity (Stealth)</li><li>Presence (Deception)</li><li>Thievery Trade</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "UQMIR0G36A5Y12FE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Street Rat", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/mammals/rodent-rat-diseaed-gray.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>To become a thief, one must have a certain level of determination and focus to allow delicate acts quickly and with a high variety of unpredictability. One must also know every trick in the book to get themselves out of danger and into your pockets.</p><p>As a street rat, you gain the following Thief abilities:</p><p><strong>Thief&rsquo;s Focus (1 Finger)</strong></p><p>When making a Sleight of Hand or Stealth check, before knowing the result, you can spend 1 Finger to increase the result by +5.</p><p><strong>Catch!</strong></p><p>You can pass an item no heavier than 6 lbs to another creature up to 20 ft away. So long as the creature can see you, is willing, and is capable, they automatically catch the item.</p><p><strong>Quaff</strong></p><p>You can drink any potion or potion-sized drink as a Minor Action instead of an Action.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "I3ZGJ4PULFJFHGD3", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Book of Spells", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/trades/academics-book-study-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>An essential tool for many Wizards is their spellbook. It is where all their most important research regarding the nature of magic and the universe around them is written down.</p><p>When first taking this Wizard Ability, the Wizard hits a breakthrough, and casts a one-time ritual spell to create the spellbook from scratch. As part of this process, they choose the design of the spellbook&rsquo;s cover and binding. When the book is created, it contains your arcane scrawlings on all of the spells you know, and you add to this spellbook as you learn new ones.</p><p><strong>Your Spellbook</strong></p><p>Any spellbook you create can function as an arcane focus for you, and so long as you channel your spells into it as part of a long rest all of the spells you know are automatically prepared instead of having to choose.</p><p>In addition, if you are in possession of any spell scrolls or spellpages, you can tuck them between the pages of your spellbook to temporarily add a number of spells up to your proficiency bonus to your spellbook. These spells must be of a level which you can cast, and they remain prepared until you channel again. Tucked spell scrolls are not destroyed when their spell is cast in this way.</p><p>Each spellbook is inherently linked to the wizard who wrote it. As such, Wizards cannot prepare or cast spells from another wizard&rsquo;s spellbook. Should you find yourself in possession of another wizard&rsquo;s spellbook, you may be able to make use of some of its contents as described in the <em>Salvaging a Spellbook</em> section.</p><p><strong>Treatise</strong></p><p>When you select this ability, you also gain a loose spellpage containing one Wizard spell you don&rsquo;t already know that is of a level you could learn.</p><p><strong>Replacing a Spellbook</strong></p><p>Because of their mystical construction, spellbooks are highly resistant to most natural elements; they do not easily burn, soak, or tear, and any such damage is magically mended the next time it is channeled, if the damage is not too severe. However, it is not unheard of for a Wizard&rsquo;s spellbook to be rendered unrepairable in extreme circumstances. When a spellbook is destroyed, any loose spell scrolls or spellpages tucked inside are destroyed with it.</p><p>Should a Wizard lose their spellbook and have to write a new one, they can do so as a <em>Long Rest Action</em> with a new and empty spellbook or any suitable medium&mdash;though any improvised option will be less durable than a proper spellbook. During this process, they can copy down all of the spells they know. Spells that you don&rsquo;t know but had temporarily prepared due to spell scrolls or spellpages that were tucked into your old spellbook are not recovered.</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.rest-actions.J5UBBMIM6FKPUK1C]{Replace Spellbook}</p><p><strong>Salvaging a Spellbook</strong></p><p>Because of the arcane bond between a wizard and their spellbook, as well as the inscrutable proprietary scrawlings made by the wizard for each spell, other wizards cannot cast spells from another wizard&rsquo;s spellbook.</p><p>Instead, wizards can perform a 1 minute ritual to carefully separate one spell&rsquo;s page from a spellbook, turning it into a discrete spellpage for use in tucking into your spellbook, as described above. Unfortunately, this separation process destroys the spellbook in the process.</p><p><strong>Sharing Spells</strong></p><p>While many wizards closely guard their accumulated arcane secrets for fear of what could come about were they to fall into the wrong hands, collaboration between wizards can lead to even greater knowledge. As a <em>Rest Action</em>, you can copy one Wizard spell you know onto a discrete spellpage, should you have one in your possession.</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.rest-actions.1ZTDHXICI9AG8MH1]{Sharing Spells}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "novice"}, "requirements": "Must have the Wizard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "L4TCBW3PWUZVSULN", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Efforless Cantrips", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-hand-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>After countless castings, your most practiced spells begin to summon forth like a reflex; effortlessly and with startling quickness. </em></p><p>Whenever you cast a cantrip with one or more charge options applied to it, reduce its total mana cost by 1 (minimum 0).</p><p>In addition, when a creature triggers an attack of opportunity from you, you can use your reaction to cast a cantrip at the creature instead of making a weapon attack. The cantrip must have a casting time of 1 action or less and must only target that creature. Cantrips with a ranged spell attack do not suffer disadvantage from the target being within 5ft of you when cast using this ability.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "adept"}, "requirements": "6th level overall and 3rd level Wizard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "ZG3FXZY4IZX4LH6N", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Eustress", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-beam-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>When fate hangs in the balance, you abandon caution and push your wizardry to its absolute limit. </em></p><p>When you use a Desperate Action to cast a spell, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>Your Charge Limit for this casting of the spell is increased by 1.</li><li>You can choose to take a level of @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion} to reduce the spell&rsquo;s base mana cost to 0.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Must have a Wizard Adept Ability", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "SHD2ABFLNZ9CNNII", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "School of Study", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-stack.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As you get your feet under you as a Wizard, you naturally gravitate toward certain schools of magic, specializing in the spells and capabilities innate to that school. Pick one school of magic to specialize in:</p><ul><li><em>Abjuration</em></li><li><em>Conjuration</em></li><li><em>Divination</em></li><li><em>Evocation</em></li><li><em>Illusion</em></li><li><em><em>Mesmerization</em></em></li><li><em>Necromancy</em></li><li><em>Transmutation </em></li></ul><p>Each time you cast a spell from your chosen school of magic you gain the following bonuses:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Gain a +1 bonus on one of the spell&rsquo;s spell attack modifiers.</li><li>Gain a +1 bonus on one of the spell save DCs for that spell.</li></ul><p>In addition, based on your chosen school, you learn Spell Charges that can be used with any spell, and gain a unique bonus to all spells that you cast with that school. These Spell School Bonuses can be found beneath this section.</p><p><em>Learning New Schools of Study:</em> You become an expert in 1 additional School of Study at each of the following:</p><ul><li>The first of either Spellcaster level 8 or Wizard level 6.</li><li>The first of either Spellcaster level 16 or Wizard level 12.</li><li>Wizard level 18.</li></ul><h3>Spell School Bonuses</h3><p><strong>Abjuration</strong></p><p>The following Spell Charges are now options for any reasonably applicable spell:</p><ul><li>1 Mana: Spells that have area effects can be manipulated to cause some or all creatures to not be affected by the spell.</li></ul><p>When you cast an Abjuration spell, you can choose to apply this additional effect:</p><ul><li>Gain temporary hit points equal to twice the mana spent on the spell, adding on top of any you already have. Afterward, if the spell targets a creature other than you, you can also transfer any number of your temporary hit points to them.</li></ul><p><strong>Conjuration</strong></p><p>The following Spell Charges are now options for any reasonably applicable spell:</p><ul><li>1 Mana: You briefly conjure a lesser spirit that will deliver this spell instead of you. <br />The lesser spirit can be conjured anywhere you can see within 60 ft of you. However, if the spell has a range of touch, the Mana cost increases by 1, and spirit can only be conjured within 30 ft of you. <br />The spirit dissipates after the spell is cast, when struck mid-casting, or when the spellcasting is otherwise prevented. <br />If the spirit is dissipated before it can cast the spell, then you can cast it from yourself instead and may select a different target if the original is no longer targetable.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>When you cast a Conjuration spell, you can choose to apply this additional effect:</p><ul><li>Conjure a <em>Conjured Wisp</em> at the target point of the spell. The wisp has no senses, but it is under your complete control, acting on your turn.</li></ul><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Conjured Wisp</strong></p><p><em>Tiny Elemental</em></p><p>Armor Class: 10</p><p>Hit Points: 1</p><p>Writer: Hudson Bielstein</p><p>Speed: Float 30 ft.</p><p>Challenge: 0 (0 XP)</p><p>Str - 1 (-5) | Dex - 1 (-5) | Con - 1 (-5)</p><p>Int - 1 (-5) | Wis 1 (-5) | Pres - 1 (-5)</p><p>Senses: None</p><p>Skills: --</p><p>Languages: --</p><p><em>Wisp</em>: The wisp glows just enough to be seen in the dark. It cannot use the assist action.</p><p><em>Wisp of Burden: </em>A wisp can surround and magically carry an object weighing no more than 2 lbs.&nbsp;</p><p><em>Disperse</em>: When the wisp moves into another creature, it can dissipate and deal 1 psychic damage as a non-action.</p><p><em>Fleeting</em>: Conjured wisps dissipate automatically after 1 hour.</p><p>Actions in Combat</p><p>Flare: As an action, the wisp can dissipate to cast 15ft of bright light and an additional 15ft of dim light from where it dissipated. This light lasts until the would-be start of its next turn.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Divination</strong></p><p>The following Spell Charges are now options for any reasonably applicable spell:</p><ul><li>1 Mana: Choose one creature affected by the spell. Increase or decrease the result of the chosen creature&rsquo;s next roll by 2.</li></ul><p>When you cast a Divination spell, you can choose to apply this additional effect:</p><ul><li>If this spell costs mana, choose a creature you can see, roll a d20, look at it, and set the result aside. Within the next 10 minutes, the next d20 roll made by that creature is replaced by the result you rolled instead. You cannot use this ability again until the d20 you set aside is used or the 10 minutes are up, whichever comes first.</li></ul><p><strong>Mesmerization</strong></p><p>The following Spell Charges are now options for any reasonably applicable spell:</p><ul><li>1 Mana: You do not provoke attacks of opportunity from the targets of this spell this turn.</li><li>1 Mana: Choose one creature affected by the spell. The target must make a Wisdom (Save) check. On a failure, the creature&rsquo;s movement speeds become 0. <br />Flying creatures remain aloft or glide to the nearest stable footing if they are capable of doing so.</li><li>1 Mana: Choose one creature affected by the spell. The target must make a Wisdom (Save) check. On a failure, you can force them to move their full speed toward or away from you at the start of their next turn, taking the safest route to do so.</li></ul><p>When you cast a Mesmerization spell, you can choose to apply these additional effects:</p><ul><li>If this spell does not charm the target, the creature must make a Wisdom (Save) check against your spell save DC or become @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed}&nbsp;for 1 minute. The charm ends early if you or one of your allies attacks the creature. When the spell ends, the creature knows it was charmed by you.</li><li>While a creature is @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed}&nbsp;by you, it cannot knowingly harm creatures you designate.</li></ul><p><strong>Evocation</strong></p><p>The following Spell Charges are now options for any reasonably applicable spell:</p><ul><li>1 Mana: One of the spell&rsquo;s damage rolls deals 5 additional damage of the same damage type.</li></ul><p>When you cast an Evocation spell, you can choose to apply this additional effect:</p><ul><li>You can reroll 1s on any of your dice rolled as part of this spell, except for 1s rolled on d20s.</li></ul><p><strong>Illusion</strong></p><p>The following Spell Charges are now options for any reasonably applicable spell:</p><ul><li>1 Mana: When you cast a spell, you can make it appear like it came from a creature adjacent to you instead.  If the spell would apply a mental effect like @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed}&nbsp;or @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.UK95BQ45TGSD5Q3V]{Frightened}, then these apply as if the adjacent creature cast the spell instead.</li></ul><p>When you cast an Illusion spell, you can choose to apply this additional effect:</p><ul><li>You create an illusory duplicate of yourself for 1 minute. The duplicate is controlled by you, acting on your turn with the same movement speed. When you speak or make any other sound (such as clapping) then your duplicate emits the same audio. For the duration, both you and the duplicate appear illusory, being slightly blurry and translucent so as to appear indistinguishable. <br />When one of you is attacked or otherwise touched, struck, or injured, flip a coin. If heads, that figure was you and the event is carried out like normal. As a result, your duplicate dissipates. If tails, that figure was your illusory duplicate. Any interaction passes through it, causing it to dissipate. <br />If one of you would take an action that would affect the surroundings, the other you dissipates, revealing the acting figure to be the real one.<br />If your illusory double dissipates from time running out, choose which one was yourself the whole time.<br />The double does not confuse creatures that rely on senses other than sight or sound.</li></ul><p><strong>Necromancy</strong></p><p>The following Spell Charges are now options for any reasonably applicable spell:</p><ul><li>2 Mana: When you cast a spell that requires a Constitution (Save) check, you can attempt to drain the vigor from one target. If the chosen creature fails the spell&rsquo;s first Constitution (Save) check, you can choose to sap either its Strength or Dexterity. Until the target takes a long rest, that attribute of theirs is decreased by 1. Until you take a long rest, that attribute of yours is increased by 1. <br />Keep track of your original attribute scores and update your modifier accordingly.</li></ul><p>When you cast a Necromancy spell, <em>or</em> when an undead creature under your control hits a creature with an attack, you can choose to apply this additional effect:</p><ul><li>As a reaction, you can use one 1 of your rest dice to deal additional necrotic damage. Roll the chosen rest die and deal necrotic damage to the target equal to the result.  Additionally, you can cause one creature within 10ft of the target to restore an equal amount of hit points.</li></ul><p><strong>Transmutation</strong></p><p>The following Spell Charges are now options for any reasonably applicable spell:</p><ul><li>1 Mana: You can enchant a non-living item or 5ft space with the effects of this spell. After completing the casting time of the spell, it is applied to the chosen target within the spell&rsquo;s range, but delays the spell's effect to trigger when the item or surface is touched by a creature. As part of the casting, you can designate up to 3 creatures to be unable to trigger the effect. The target is not highlighted by this enchantment, so creatures without some ability to detect magic would not see what was enchanted, even if they saw you casting the enchantment.<br />When the enchantment is triggered, the triggering creature becomes the target of the spell's effects. When triggered by a creature unawares, the spell&rsquo;s first spell attack has advantage to hit, and the target has disadvantage against its first spell save.<br />If not triggered within 10 minutes of being placed, the enchantment dissipates.</li></ul><p>When you cast a Transmutation spell, you can choose to apply this additional effect:</p><ul><li>The duration of this spell is doubled, if its duration is not instantaneous.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "novice"}, "requirements": "Must have the Wizard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "RFBX1FZ2ALJA5G3Z", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spellcasting (Wizard)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/rune-sigil-black-pink.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Wizards use arcane means to formulate spells that bend the world to their will. What is deemed mythical or impossible to many, Wizards view as elementary calculations of science. Mathematics, physics, alchemy, magic&mdash;all are equally capable of using and breaking down the laws of the universe to allow feats once thought impossible.</p><p><strong>Cantrips</strong></p><p>Upon gaining your 1st level of Wizard, you know three Cantrips from the Wizard&rsquo;s spell list. You gain an additional Cantrip when you first reach Adept Wizard, and then another at Expert Wizard.</p><p><strong>Spells at 1st Level</strong></p><p>At 1st level, your mind bursts with magical inspiration, quickly discovering and memorizing six 1st level spells of your choice from the Wizard&rsquo;s spell list to permanently know.</p><p><strong>Mana</strong></p><p>Wizards, like all spellcasters, expend Mana to cast spells (expanded upon in the Mana section of <strong>&ldquo;Chapter 9: Magic &amp; Spellcasting&rdquo;</strong>). They regain all spent Mana after a long rest, and half of their maximum Mana on a short rest.</p><p><strong>Arcane Spellcasting Focus</strong></p><p>You may use an arcane focus, a specialized item used to channel and cast spells, as a spellcasting focus for casting your Wizard spells.</p><p>While in the Wizard&rsquo;s possession, a spellcasting focus allows spells to be cast without most material components. Material components that have a cost or are said to be used up by the spell cannot be replaced using an arcane focus.</p><p><strong>Preparing and Casting Spells</strong></p><p>Wizards, unlike other spellcasters, must use an arcane focus, a specialized item used for casting, in order to prepare or cast their complex Wizard spells.</p><p>A Wizard channels a series of spells into their spellcasting focus from their known spells. These become the list of spells available to them while wielding it, and they lose access to casting those spells while the focus is not in their possession. They do this by, each long rest, selecting a number of known Wizard spells to prepare equal to:</p><ul><li>Your Wizard level + your Intelligence modifier. (Minimum of 1)</li></ul><p>This channeling is personal and lasts until they channel again&mdash;no two spellcasting foci can store your prepared spells at once, and other Wizards cannot cast your spells using your arcane focus.</p><p>The spells the Wizard prepares are available to be cast until they decide to prepare another spell in its place. A Wizard can change the spells they have prepared at the end of a long rest.</p><p>Note: To figure out how many and what spells you know, reference the <strong>Spells at 1st Level</strong> above this section, and if needed, the <strong>Learning Spells at Higher Levels </strong>section below this one.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability</strong></p><p>Being that you obtain your magic ability through intense study and memorization, Intelligence is the spellcasting ability for a Wizard. Meaning that your Intelligence modifier comes into play when setting the DC for your Wizard spells and when making an attack with one.</p><ul><li><em>Spell Save DC: </em>8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier&nbsp;</li></ul><ul><li><em>Spell Attack Modifier: </em>your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier</li></ul><p><strong>Ritual Casting</strong></p><p>You can cast a Wizard spell as a Ritual if that spell has the Ritual tag and you know the spell. You do not need to have the spell prepared when casting a spell this way.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Wizard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "RGKNFQH7M4AJXSXV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Wizard Spells", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-runed-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>1st level Wizards get access to Wizard Magic, which consists of 1st through 7th level spells.  However, you do not have access to all of them right away.  These spell levels become accessible as follows:</p><p><i>Wizard Spell Levels</i></p><table><tr><th>Spell Level</th><th>Unlock Requirements</th></tr><tr><td>Level 1 Spells</td><td>1st Level Wizard.</td></tr><tr><td>Level 2 Spells</td><td>2nd Level Wizard;<br>3rd Level Overall.</td></tr><tr><td>Level 3 Spells</td><td>3rd Level Wizard;<br>5th Level Overall<br>(At least 4 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 4 Spells</td><td>4th Level Wizard;<br>7th Level Overall<br>(At least 6 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 5 Spells</td><td>5th Level Wizard;<br>9th Level Overall<br>(At least 8 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 6 Spells</td><td>6th Level Wizard;<br>11th Level Overall<br>(At least 10 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 7 Spells</td><td>7th Level Wizard;<br>13th Level Overall<br>(At least 12 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Wizard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "U2NS38QP7TBT6SMG", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Twin Charge", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/symbol-lightning-bolt.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>A spell is nothing more than a template waiting to be reshaped to your exacting demands.</em></p><p>Whenever you cast a spell, you can apply up to two charge effects to it instead of one.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "adept"}, "requirements": "6th level overall and 3rd level Wizard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "DNKUZOHBFP8JQ80N", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Battle Trance", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As a minor action on your turn once per long rest, you close your eyes and exhale, putting yourself into a state of self-induced hypnosis. Through a mental technique passed down through generations, you distance yourself from reality in preparation for the violence of combat. As you open your eyes again, you act purely on instinct, becoming @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.Y822OUCDEPAG0HS8]{Frenzied}. <br />At the end of each turn, you can attempt to make a DC 13 Wisdom (Save) check to end the frenzy. <br />Frenzied conditions entered this way do not benefit from the Calm Mind racial trait, but also do not break your spell concentration.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "0YDXA4M4W7KKFZM1", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Calm Mind", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have advantage on save checks to resist falling into a negative emotional state, such as those caused by @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.UK95BQ45TGSD5Q3V]{Frightened} or @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.Y822OUCDEPAG0HS8]{Frenzied}.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "WLAJ2YWVGZC2NL8Y", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Helix Wings", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have an array of strong feathers attached to a rotor-like hub beneath your neck. By flexing a core muscle, this hub can be rotated at extreme speed, with the angled feathers creating lift in a form akin to a helicopter. You have a flying speed of 25 feet. <br />To use this speed, you cannot be wearing medium or heavy armor.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "KYSYXGJ0975JHGQV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "High Altitude Adaption", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are adapted to being above the clouds, and do not suffer adverse effects of being in those environments.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "SWQIHGVCC7ULP8LY", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Feather Cloak", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have large and extended tuft feathers that drape down to your shins. By ruffling your feathers, you can widen your feathers together and close any gaps to act as a parachute. So long as you are not <strong>incapacitated</strong>, you can land on your feet and prevent yourself from taking falling damage when falling.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "K209GDHAKHLWD2ZO", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Feathered Furore", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As you lack the ability to fly, you have grown more capable in the wielding of your wings and feathers in turn.<br />As an action, choose two items or pieces of equipment held or strapped on to a creature, aside from armor. That creature must make a Strength (Save) check of DC 10 + your Proficiency Bonus. On failure, the creature must choose which of the two things you listed to let go of, as the wind catches it and flings up to 30ft in a direction of your choosing.<br />You regain the usage of this ability at the end of a long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "MWI5F41P3AGMTOBP", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Short-Distance Flier", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you use your flying speed, you must land at the end of your turn.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "5Q2XHBBE46MGKS0R", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Storm Acclimatized", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your Feather Cloak is weatherproof, and your talons are gripped, allowing you to be able to ignore penalties from heavy rain.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "T3GAI02T73XXHXOT", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Storm Starter", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>At 5th level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.UEGGABQ79I8A8CG5]{Twister} spell adjacent to you once per long rest. When cast this way, you automatically succeed the twister Strength (Save) check unless you choose to fail it.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "RR6BVPL9LOV2HAXV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Wicked Wind", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace one of your attacks with a swirl of your extended and sharpened neck feathers that lifts you 5ft in the air before immediately dropping back down. When you do this, each creature within a 5ft radius must make a Dexterity saving throw of DC = 8 + your Constitution modifier + your proficiency bonus. On a failed save, a creature takes 1d8 slashing damage. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage. <br />This damage increases by 1d8 when you reach 5th level (2d8), 11th level (3d8), and 17th level (4d8).<br />You can use Wicked Wind a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "AE4EGB6H1CSLN85E", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Cutting Vortex", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Once you reach 5th level, you gain the following racial trait. <br />As an action, you give a harsh spin of your wings that detaches up to 5 feather darts (taking 1 chaos damage for each) to create a 5ft twister adjacent to you. The vortex violently spins with sharpened feathers for 1 minute or until a large enough gust of wind can disperse it. <br />Any creature who moves into the vortex&rsquo;s space on their turn, or else starts their turn inside of it, takes 1d4 slashing damage for each feather dart used to make the vortex.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "H7QEVR59YLDQIPH3", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Feather Dart", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You grow 10 sharpened feather darts growing in your plume. As a minor action, you can pluck up to three of these, taking 1 hit point of damage for each. Each plucked feather is equivalent to the Dart weapon, but breaks after a single use.<br />Upon completing a long rest, any plucked feather darts grow back.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "WHIWHF415AFOHZO3", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Bird of Prey", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have long, sharp, curved talons on your hands and feet. These can be used as a natural weapon that deals 1d6 slashing damage.<br />When you succeed on a contested Grapple check against a creature, you may additionally deal the damage of your talon natural weapon, but as piercing damage instead.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "VHIDDMOZ69USKFHW", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Feather Pockets", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>The feather muscles on your arms are more dexterous than most. You can hide up to four tiny items in your feathers, flexing your feather muscles to hold them in place. These small items can be no larger or heavier than two gold coins each. </p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "CMXV21DFSWEDTHUC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Corpse Casting", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.44UXH5FVH6EK2UI9]{Disuse Atrophy} cantrip at will. At 3rd level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.V4RW5MFB4N243CDA]{Open Wounds} spell once per long rest. At 5th level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.DS8BAOY19DVGW5SH]{Stupefy} spell once per long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "DSGZMV7CBP9IKHPD", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Element Flail", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Of all parts of a Zhier, the tail is the point most connected to its spirit element. You can swing your tail like a natural weapon flail. This weapon has both the Light and Finesse properties, and deals 1d4 damage of the damage type associated with your Spirit Element.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}, "attribute": "str", "actionType": "mwak", "chatFlavor": "", "damage": {"parts": [["1d4 + @mod", "same damage type as Spirit Element"]], "versatile": ""}, "properties": {"amm": false, "fin": true, "foc": false, "hvy": false, "lgt": true, "lod": false, "rch": false, "spc": false, "thr": false, "two": false, "una": false, "ver": false}, "proficient": true, "showInAttacks": true}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "3QPFSY40NDIM3XL9", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Howl", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can project a howl up to a mile away.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "XRZMC82H6U0DER0Y", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Inhuman", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Zhier are considered Beasts, and only Beasts, when it comes to rules affecting creatures types.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "EQWTTLVYL3B2EALU", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Light Mount", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can carry a single creature that is at least one size smaller than you on your back without reducing your movement speed. If this creature is wearing heavy armor, your movement speed is halved.<br />As long as the creature on your back is not encumbered, the weight of their body and equipment does not count against your carrying capacity. If they are encumbered, only the weight they are carrying in excess of their own carrying capacity is counted against yours. <br />Creatures can spend 5 feet of movement to get onto your back, so long as you are willing. Alternatively, you can spend a minor action to pull a willing creature that is at least one size smaller than you on or off of your back.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "T147SCK0L9JBNDJ4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mouth Grip", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can use your mouth to grip or interact with something as if as a hand. For example, you can wield one-handed weapons in your mouth, handle an object or magic item, or open doors. However, complex items take twice as long to use, and Loading weapons now require a minor action to be reloaded at the end of your turn.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2AAUZETAFQSEKV9M", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Quadruped", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are a quadrupedal creature, walking on four legs. You also have no arms to wield weapons, cast spells, control a mount, or otherwise interact with objects that require hands or arms.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "1TYQ7CP70PTQ1KLX", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Somatic Tail", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>So long as your tail is unrestrained, it can be used to fulfill the somatic component of spells.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "US9E7VG69DJXD7WX", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spirit Casting Additional Trait (Cold)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Once per day, when you cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.KH6D03TEJYZNA62N]{Cold Snap} cantrip, you can charge the spell as if you spent 1 extra mana in casting it.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "O27T8DMCLZPKT1W3", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spirit Casting Additional Trait (Fire)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>At 3rd level, once per day, when you cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.58I1UTE8ZV4CJ5W6]{Adherent Embers} cantrip, you can charge the spell as if you spent 1 extra mana in casting it.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "VFSHRL6BWD7HQMXQ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spirit Casting Additional Trait (Lightning)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>At 3rd level, once per day, when you cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.37VLMG8DVH1QVCYM]{Conduit Shock} spell, you can charge the spell as if you spent 1 extra mana in casting it.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "6HMQFQZ7A29OJEGP", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spirit Casting Additional Trait (Poison)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>At 3rd level, once per day, when you cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.MB7NWQ5H11LSIVV7]{Caustic Needle}, you can charge the spell as if you spent 1 extra mana in casting it.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "YJYHZV2J65GS21QS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spirit Casting (Cold)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.KH6D03TEJYZNA62N]{Cold Snap} cantrip. At 5th level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.IJWDFSYAAI44S9JD]{Frigid Barrage} spell once per long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "J5UHXN59MY3NP3VV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spirit Casting (Fire)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.58I1UTE8ZV4CJ5W6]{Adherent Embers} cantrip. The embers created by the spell float near your tail until used. At 5th level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.7UWC00HNXCOL4GFI]{Fireball} spell once per long rest.&nbsp;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "OCP4C1AL9OIF3NRK", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spirit Casting (Lightning)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.0JWJ9J7A2AMSNDK0]{Jolt} cantrip. You can also cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.37VLMG8DVH1QVCYM]{Conduit Shock} spell once per long rest.&nbsp;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "YNBPIYB4O41QRD6N", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spirit Casting (Poison)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.MB7NWQ5H11LSIVV7]{Caustic Needle} cantrip, dealing poison damage instead of acid when cast in this way. At 3rd level, you can cast the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.IGNXR8HBQZS1JVCY]{Ophidian Kiss}<em></em> spell once per long rest.&nbsp;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "15AYWYZJLABDJ09Z", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Strong Jaw", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can wield heavy and two-handed weapons in your jaw, so long as the weapon is not ranged or has the loading property. <br />While wielding weapons with the versatile trait, you can tighten or loosen your grip to to be considered as holding the weapon with two hands or one hand, respectively.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "AABF3VD0XLSXJW60", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Ethereal Jaunt", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As an action, you can briefly transform yourself and up to one willing creature you are carrying into an ethereal form made of strong winds and vapors that travel along the ground. You immediately escape all physical restraints, and can remain intangible until the end of your turn. While you are in this form, your movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity and you gain resistance to all damage types. You can also pass through narrow openings no smaller than an inch, moving at half speed if the gap is smaller than a foot.<br />Additionally, you can move through all other creatures as if they were difficult terrain, and the first time you move through each creature this turn it must make a Dexterity (Save) check versus 8 + your Dexterity (Acrobatics) bonus or take 2d6 slashing damage on a failed save or half as much on a success. If you have the Zhier ability &ldquo;<em>Spirit Element</em>,&rdquo; then it can make the damage type be that of your <em>Spirit Element</em> instead.<br />You can use this trait once per long rest. If you are occupying the same space as another creature when the effect ends, you are shoved into the nearest unoccupied space.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Ether Jaunt", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 1, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "OFPN9HTKWIHFGJII", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Voice on the Wind", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can project your voice to be heard and understood at twice the normal distance, and noise created by strong winds can never drown out the sound of your voice.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "9JN3KP9RXNJ1UWZJ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Armored Spine", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have a set of keratin scales layered along your spine, giving you extra protection where it counts. While not wearing armor, your Armor Class is 13 + your Dexterity Modifier (Max 2).</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "7XEVJ8IGYPAM7913", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Looped Locomotion", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As a minor action, you can leap and curl into a loop so that you begin rolling on your armored spine. While you are in this wheel form, you gain a +1 bonus to your AC. The only actions you can take while in wheel form are the <strong>Dash</strong>, <strong>Disengage</strong>, <strong>Saving a Target</strong>, and <strong>Self-Defense</strong> actions, and you can leave wheel form as a minor action or by falling @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.RK3DF56CKMQUV6DM]{Prone}. If you start your turn in wheel form, your walking speed is increased by 10ft until the end of your turn.<br />While in wheel form, if you roll at least 15ft in a straight line immediately before ramming into a creature, they must make a Dexterity (Save) check versus 8 + your Strength (Athletics) bonus. On a failed save, the creature takes 1d6 bludgeoning damage per 15ft you traveled this turn before the collision (max 3d6) and you immediately exit your wheel form.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "YW7J3KWFP497JP5P", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Lunar Affinity", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While in direct moonlight, you gain +1 to all checks.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "UEBZ9LPMH9YWUEKM", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Lunar Cycle", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your connection to the moon shifts each night, changing in much the same way that the moon&rsquo;s visage does, but at a faster pace. This connection cycles between two phases; New Moon and Full Moon. These phases manifest visually as an uncanny specular sheen to your fur. While in Full Moon phase, your fur has a faint front-lighting regardless of the light source. Meanwhile, in New Moon phase, an underglow surrounds your face and body. <br />You start in the New Moon phase, and each long rest you swap to the phase you aren&rsquo;t currently in. Your other magical gifts as a lunar zhier are heavily influenced by which phase you are in when you use them.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": "New Moon", "style": "choice", "name": "Lunar Phase", "valueFrom": "manual", "maxFormula": "", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "reminder", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "Swap phases", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "zhier-lunar-cycle", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": ["New Moon", "Full Moon"]}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "6C0WDIXDL8N1AQSG", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Nocturnal Light", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.NTGJ71IJ1VDA3GS9]{Luminescence} cantrip. The light you cast with this spell resembles moonlight, and its brightness is determined by your Lunar Cycle phase.<ul><li><strong>New Moon phase:</strong> Your @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.NTGJ71IJ1VDA3GS9]{Luminescence} cantrip only sheds 30 feet of dim light.</li><li><strong>Full Moon phase:</strong> Your @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.NTGJ71IJ1VDA3GS9]{Luminescence} cantrip only sheds 30 feet of bright light.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "5JTXJQ589XY9XY1R", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Transient Magic", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>At 5th level, your connection to the moon grows stronger, allowing you to draw upon a selection of powerful spells determined by your Lunar Cycle phase. You regain the ability to use this trait when you finish a long rest.<ul><li><strong>New Moon phase:</strong> You can cast either the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.Z373UKDNQ9VFAMQD]{Syzygy} or @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.XD6W9NSEKZ48HGCD]{Dispel Magic} spell once with this trait.</li><li><strong>Full Moon phase:</strong> You can cast either the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.6GFN59MWTZPMBQ61]{Haste} or @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.FOW5GSST2ZXRMKJ4]{Illusory Creature} spell once with this trait.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "9YZ9MU6RHEEIME77", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Resplendent Flail", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>If you have the @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.3QPFSY40NDIM3XL9]{Element Flail} zhier racial trait, increase the damage of the tail natural weapon by one die size.<ul><li>Otherwise, you have a tail with a vibrant tuft of fur at its tip. You can swing it at targets as a natural weapon flail. This weapon has the Finesse property and deals 1d4 radiant damage. On impact, it sears your target and scatters specks of sunlight.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "5I4QJNLLGII5HT53", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Solar Surge", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have a number of surge charges equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended charges on a long rest. Each time you hit a target with an attack, you can spend a surge charge to make a natural weapon attack with your tail as a non-action. <br />You can choose to chain surge attacks together until you either miss or run out of charges to spend.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}, "resource": {"showOnSheet": true, "value": 0, "style": "counter", "name": "Solar Surge", "valueFrom": "formula", "maxFormula": "@prof", "maxFlat": 0, "rechargeOn": "long", "rechargeStyle": "fill", "rechargeFormula": "", "rechargeMessage": "", "overfilledMessage": "", "dropdownIdentifier": "", "addOptionsTo": "", "dropdownOptions": []}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "SEVHM17XUDB3QKR1", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sunbathe", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Once per long rest, as a rest action, you can sunbathe in direct sunlight to soak up energy from the sun to regain expended @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.SEVHM17XUDB3QKR1]{Solar Surge} charges equal to half your proficiency bonus. In addition, your fur begins to glow, shedding 10ft of dim light until you expend your last @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.SEVHM17XUDB3QKR1]{Solar Surge} charge or get an hour into a long rest.</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.rest-actions.486ZS1ZZY5HJU1H5]{Sunbathe}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "NIR7W2U5N0DVWX8Z", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
